{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware","id":1225302,"title":"Art, Criticism and Freedom. (Contains Disturbing Topics, Please Be Aware)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-06T08:59:07-07:00","id":1225302,"title":"Art, Criticism and Freedom. (Contains Disturbing Topics, Please Be Aware)","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/411718-inspirational-art-exalted-3e-edition?p=1225284#post1225284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know what that film is about, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As to not further derail the Inspirational thread...<br /> <br /> I do Isator, I find it abhorent. Never watched it, and probably never will.<br /> <br /> I would if I had academic objectives around it, like if I was a film student, or studied race relations. But I don't.<br /> <br /> You know that this year's film festivals featured films of intense violence, sexual and otherwise, visited including on children, right? To critical acclaim, right? There are extremely graphic and heavy movies being produced today.<br /> <br /> I really don't understand people that would subject themselves to that.<br /> <br /> I will never consume that. Not even in cartoons, much less live action.<br /> <br /> But I will never argue for total censorship.<br /> <br /> Restrict age of attendance, exhibition venue and hours, include disclaimers? Totally for it.<br /> <br /> Censorship? Never. The cost is immeasurable.<br /> <br /> I don't even consider myself an old school tough guy, you know? I'm squeamish as hell. Hate gore horror, never watch it. I cry all the time in Holocaust movies, and everytime I see the Passion of the Christ, even not being religious myself. And since I'm being completely honest here, some Disney movies too (I hate you Mufasa).<br /> <br /> But the old adage &quot;sticks and stones...&quot; rings true for me.<br /> <br /> As long as people aren't harassing you to expose you to things you don't like, I don't believe you have any case to restrict what they want to say.<br /> <br /> <u><i><b>DISCLAIMER:</b></i></u><br /> <br /> This is NOT the &quot;Female Sexual Objectification in Fantasy Art Discussion&quot; thread.<br /> <br /> Talking about this in a thread about freedom to produce and consume art, and the proper time and place to criticize such art, is just screaming &quot;THINK OF THE CHILDREN!&quot;. It is not central to the topic at hand, and is thread drift.<br /> <br /> This discussion is intended to be philosophical (drivel?) about freedom to produce and consume art, when and where to criticize it. If you want to argue that it is always right to criticize &quot;harmful art&quot;, that is a fair point, and we can dive into what makes art harmful, who decides said art is harmful etc...<br /> <br /> DO NOT BRING ANYONES SPECIFIC ISSUES INTO IT. They will be considered thread drift and treated as such.<br /> <br /> Please read the topic and first post to confirm what THIS thread is about.<br /> <br /> Please understand that discussion of any other matters is shifting the topic. Which I am very nonchalant about and will engage however I understand is appropriate.<br /> <br /> DO NOTE that I will not bring my issues into a platform you create to discuss your issues, as I do realize that is impolite and against the forum rules.<br /> <br /> I DO NOT CARE about your rules about why you are free to shift topics but I am not. Unless you are an elightened debater armed with objective truth, THIS WILL NOT CHANGE.<br /> <br /> If you need to label me anything you want and feel a need to tell me about it, I simply request you respect the rules and do not insult me while you're at it. I would also appreciate if you re examine these specific needs of yours, and check if anyone else already expressed similar things, before you post. If you decide not to post, that will be good, as you won't waste your time posting, and I won't waste my time refuting what you said.<br /> <br /> If you feel anything I said is against the forum rules, please invite a moderator to the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 06-12-2018, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T09:04:41-07:00","id":1225307,"title":"","content":"Cross-posted in the image thread with the creation of this one, I'll probably delete it and post some images there instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/411718-inspirational-art-exalted-3e-edition?p=1225288#post1225288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can complain all you want, my point is that this particular complaint about drawings is getting tiresome. Or, rather, the fact it keeps being brought up incessantly. At this point the impression I get is that people feel all but obligated to point it out, as if they can't just appreciate (or not appreciate) in silence. It's an annoying zeitgeist, preaching to no one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I genuinely don't want to be rude, but, uhh... I thought the point of the thread was to provide people with Exalted-appropriate images they can grab and plug into their own games?<br /> <br /> Well, my games generally feature sensibly-dressed people. A half-naked lady <i>might </i>see some use, at some point, if I'm going for a certain decadent vibe (a half-naked <i>warrior </i>lady, on the other hand, probably not, because holy shit the rules really hate it when a character tries to pull that off), but a/ I'm far more likely to be able to use someone with some goddamn clothes on, and b/ it's very easy to hit diminishing returns on images of half-naked ladies purely due to the supply-demand discrepancy.<br /> <br /> &quot;But aluminiumtrioxid, the thread does not exist to provide <i>you specifically</i> with the images you would like to see!&quot;, I hear you cry out in protest.<br /> <br /> That is reasonable.<br /> <br /> As a community resource, the thread's usefulness depends on two criteria: the first is &quot;how much do the thread's contents overlap with the actual needs of people who would use these images in their games?&quot;. Indeed, while I have my preferences, I can't <i>prove</i> that they are universal. However, there is a second issue we should take into account: &quot;how difficult is it for somebody to obtain images of a certain thing by manually scouring Pinterest and other websites?&quot;. And I would argue that by this second criterion, images of half-naked ladies tend to do pretty badly. The internet is littered with images of half-naked ladies, even with ones that are drawn in a very technically proficient manner! Therefore <s>it is our moral imperative to tell people</s> there is nothing wrong with periodically reminding people that other kinds of images exist and the thread would be well served by having those in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T09:07:54-07:00","id":1225308,"title":"","content":"Double post?<br /> Anyway, i completely agree. <br /> <br /> There's even a practical value to allowing such expressions, after the moral necessity of letting the speaker express itself, in that an open statement can be criticized, whereas a secret statement cannot.<br /> Someone silenced also has the moral high ground to argue that she is being silenced, which gives credit to tje idea no matter how good or bad.<br /> <br /> So censorship not only is unacepptable, it's also dumb.<br /> <br /> <br /> Other than that, of course, house rules prevail: feel free to ban any topic from your house or business, it's yours after all. <br /> Oh, and none of this means saying something dumb will not meet rejection. Goodness knows how many people lost jobs or businesses to a dumb statement, and that's fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T09:14:50-07:00","id":1225310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225307#post1225307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cross-posted in the image thread with the creation of this one, I'll probably delete it and post some images there instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I genuinely don't want to be rude, but, uhh... I thought the point of the thread was to provide people with Exalted-appropriate images they can grab and plug into their own games?<br /> <br /> Well, my games generally feature sensibly-dressed people. A half-naked lady <i>might </i>see some use, at some point, if I'm going for a certain decadent vibe (a half-naked <i>warrior </i>lady, on the other hand, probably not, because holy shit the rules really hate it when a character tries to pull that off), but a/ I'm far more likely to be able to use someone with some goddamn clothes on, and b/ it's very easy to hit diminishing returns on images of half-naked ladies purely due to the supply-demand discrepancy.<br /> <br /> &quot;But aluminiumtrioxid, the thread does not exist to provide <i>you specifically</i> with the images you would like to see!&quot;, I hear you cry out in protest.<br /> <br /> That is reasonable.<br /> <br /> As a community resource, the thread's usefulness depends on two criteria: the first is &quot;how much do the thread's contents overlap with the actual needs of people who would use these images in their games?&quot;. Indeed, while I have my preferences, I can't <i>prove</i> that they are universal. However, there is a second issue we should take into account: &quot;how difficult is it for somebody to obtain images of a certain thing by manually scouring Pinterest and other websites?&quot;. And I would argue that by this second criterion, images of half-naked ladies tend to do pretty badly. The internet is littered with images of half-naked ladies, even with ones that are drawn in a very technically proficient manner! Therefore <s>it is our moral imperative to tell people</s> there is nothing wrong with periodically reminding people that other kinds of images exist and the thread would be well served by having those in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>By all means, don't take my words as a condemnation of the art that you want and like. If that's how it sounded, please have my apology.<br /> <br /> My preferences are far more aligned with yours here than you imagine. I <i>like</i> the current trend of imagery, and I, literally, have zero authority over your tastes and made no affectation of having any.<br /> <br /> I made a remark on how nowadays people insist in pointing out that half naked ladies are excessive and don't make sense. That's my one and only complaint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T09:39:23-07:00","id":1225320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225310#post1225310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made a remark on how nowadays people insist in pointing out that half naked ladies are excessive and don't make sense. That's my one and only complaint.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, but the question we should ask ourselves is - <i>does repeatedly asking that question serve a useful purpose</i>?<br /> <br /> And I would argue it does! Images of sexualized women are <i>everywhere</i>. If you need one for your game, you don't need to specifically look in the thread for Exalted inspirational images. Hell, you don't even need to type in some humiliating search keyword Pinterest will no doubt silently judge you for, like &quot;sexy warrior cat woman&quot;, because &quot;sexy&quot; is treated <i>as the default</i>. If there is no constant pushback, images of half-naked women <i>will</i> consume the thread, purely because the likelihood of any piece of art being both technically proficient <i>and</i> going against the cultural default is a lot smaller than the likelihood of them just being technically proficient.<br /> <br /> And we haven't even touched on the question of consumer appeal, ie. good art that depicts a half-naked lady is probably going to be liked and shared by a lot more people than good art that depicts something with comparatively niche appeal, like a Chinese bureaucrat. Now, what this means is that even if we assume that the people who use these forums are saints who are always mindful of the implications of the things they share, they are going to to find a lot more of the former than the latter (because it is liked and shared by a lot more people, and as a consequence, it will float to the top of search results), and them being people with a functional set of eyes, the thought will inevitably cross their minds &quot;well yeah, I mean, this is a half-naked lady but holy shit it is also <i>really good art</i>, I'm sure that posting it <i>just this one time</i> is going to be fine&quot;. And then, before you even know it, the thread will once again be full of half-naked ladies even though everybody who participated <i>did</i> actively think through the implications of what they post. All it took was people thinking that good art deserves to be shared no matter the subject.<br /> <br /> (I know that this argument could be characterized as telling people that we have a moral imperative to bully those who like good art until they stop sharing it if we don't like the subject matter, but I'll have to ask you to read it a bit more charitably.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T09:41:01-07:00","id":1225321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225307#post1225307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cross-posted in the image thread with the creation of this one, I'll probably delete it and post some images there instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I genuinely don't want to be rude, but, uhh... I thought the point of the thread was to provide people with Exalted-appropriate images they can grab and plug into their own games?<br /> <br /> Well, my games generally feature sensibly-dressed people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. I've recently started running a Star Wars game, and the PCs are on Ryloth, the Twi'lek home world, where slavery is a big problem. The PCs rescued a bunch of slaves from Black Sun last session.<br /> I looked for some pictures to illustrate the session, and while google images did a fine job finding &quot;Falleen gangster&quot;, &quot;Cloakshape fighter&quot;, and &quot;Black Sun thug&quot;, typing in &quot;Twi'lek slaves&quot; gave me a ton of pictures of Twi'lek girls wearing very little, which wasn't suitable. I don't really want the players thinking this game is some kind of prurient sex fantasy on my part.<br /> I've had similar issues previously with &quot;Dark Eldar female warrior&quot;, &quot;female tech-priest&quot; and, for Exalted, &quot;Egyptian woman fantasy art&quot; and &quot;Bast fantasy art&quot; for a cat-totem Lunar character I was considering playing in our Egypt-expy-set game. I mean, it's ancient Egypt, I don't demand or want all the pictures of women to be wearing burkas, but I really could not take the ton of pictures of barely-dressed cat-girls posing provocatively seriously for the character I wanted to play.<br /> <br /> <br /> One could argue that there's a ton of art on the internet, and you could always use different art.<br /> But I think it was pretty reasonable, on that thread, to say &quot;I like the art, I don't like how little clothes they're wearing.&quot; (It's not like they said the poster should be banned for showing art they didn't like! They just said they'd prefer something different.)<br /> <br /> If it's the occasional thing it's fine. Sometimes both women and men don't wear very much. Sometimes that's the art you want.<br /> It's just that, when looking for art for my games, the whole thing being filled with over-sexualised art of women makes it quite hard to navigate to the more regularly-dressed art I want.*<br /> <br /> *Plus, you know, when it's over common sexism, body confidence issues, etc, etc, but we all know that already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T10:01:31-07:00","id":1225334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225320#post1225320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but the question we should ask ourselves is - <i>does repeatedly asking that question serve a useful purpose</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I said nothing of purpose. I claimed it's tiresome and it's not adding anything new because, well, the established audience here already knows that. That's why just about every other post has that very comment and why I said it felt tiresome.<br /> <br /> All your concerns are very valid. None of them are what I criticized...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T10:27:54-07:00","id":1225342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225334#post1225334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said nothing of purpose. I claimed it's tiresome and it's not adding anything new because, well, the established audience here already knows that. That's why just about every other post has that very comment and why I said it felt tiresome.<br /> <br /> All your concerns are very valid. None of them are what I criticized...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So it appears the only thing we disagree on is whether the tiresomeness of seeing the critique repeated outweighs its usefulness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T10:33:02-07:00","id":1225345,"title":"","content":"This thread isn't related to Exalted. Shouldn't it go into the Off-Topic forum?<br /> <br /> Edit: Oops, noticed that it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T10:35:16-07:00","id":1225348,"title":"","content":"Why are there two threads for this?<br /> <br /> \u200bYou know, on a personal note, I'll also comment on how it's worth being critical of art depicting women in extremely skimpy clothes in fantasy just because it's a bit lazy.<br /> <br /> \u200bNot just in the sense of lacking variation and going to a very basic template, but on the most basic sense of &quot;doing less work&quot;; one has all the potential for unmoored creativity that fantasy permits, and instead opts to draw as little cloth as possible. A thin strip around the chest, a skirt with a slit in it and boots, and then done.<br /> <br /> \u200bBringing up Jen before was interesting, considering that on most of the occasions in which he draws women, he puts them in elaborately layered and patterned and folded clothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T10:46:06-07:00","id":1225355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225342#post1225342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So it appears the only thing we disagree on is whether the tiresomeness of seeing the critique repeated outweighs its usefulness?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, in that particular context, the usefulness approaches zero due to the target audience.<br /> <br /> tl;dr: Yes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T10:52:59-07:00","id":1225358,"title":"","content":"I think it's worth reiterating that the comment that started this tangent had somebody saying that the art was amazing. If anything, the comment of not being a fan of scantily clad women read as a piece of context to the effect of it being something that looked so good that it got past a usual objection.<br /> <br /> \u200bUnless one was to think that my comment on the oversimplification of &quot;response to not liking something is as simple as not watching it&quot; was the insidious call for universal censorship?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T11:01:05-07:00","id":1225360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225298-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225313#post1225313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All right then.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I feel as though this is taking my point kind of literally, rather than considering the substance of what I was saying.<br /> <br /> \u200bSure, those things are valid to the question of how The Birth of a Nation is watched now, close to a hundred years after its cinematic release, at a point in time when even bigots probably need to go very far out of their way to watch it, and perhaps find more contemporary material if they wish to do so.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe point I was making was based on a consideration of how to perceive and criticise it as though it was new, in which the statement &quot;if you don't like it, don't watch it&quot; is kind of inadequate when it's something that was both contributing to a popular narrative that marginalized and oppressed a large section of the American population, and was so empowering to bigots that it sparked the revival of an actual terrorist organisation.<br /> <br /> \u200bTo be sure, it's not a point that is <i>never</i> valid. I personally don't care much for Doctor Who, haven't watched it in years, and would, as of now, be trying to not go out of my way to speak critically of it in a conversation that had nothing to do with it, or at least was not soliciting people's opinions on the subject. Doctor Who is a product in which my dislike for it and everything that stems from therein is purely a matter of personal taste, and thus it's a lot easier on myself and anybody that I might talk to if I simply devote no attention to it at all, rather than exist in a perverse state of actively and vocally disliking it.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn the other hand, I would be fairly critical of a show such as, say, Entourage, with its portrayal of that kind of Hollywood bro culture, particularly as it pertains to comparatively recent revelations about Hollywood and its attitude towards women. Where I would propose that the Harvey Weinsteins of the world readily disappeared into the midst of that society and its general background noise of low-level misogyny, such that I would have harsh words against a show that seemed to celebrate it.<br /> <br /> \u200bSomething that I think has significance to our own particular subculture.<br /> <br /> \u200bI like fantasy fiction. I like women. I would like fantasy fiction to continue making improvements with regards to representations of women, and making them feel as though they're a welcome and valued part of the subculture.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo I think that it's fair to continue being critical of a disproportionate amount of fantasy fiction that continues to represent women in ways that have issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we're living on a very convuloted time for activism in general. Everyone has something to say and a reason why they feel someone else should shut up.<br /> <br /> My wife hates sexy lady drawings, and constantly says real women don't dress like that. She is categorical in calling out &quot;sluts and hoes&quot; for the way they dress or dance. Even though when she's had a few drinks she'll do just that. But most of the time, you got yourself a good ol conservative gal. I've been trying to mellow her out a bit on that, and thankfully it has been working, but you can still feel the condescension when she talks about women with litlle clothes on the streets, specially if they're around me.<br /> <br /> My cousin is a pin-up model and draws pin-up girls in fantasy, sci-fi, western, whatever. She says shes a cock teaser, loves and is proud of it. She will tell you to eat a dick if you criticize her drawings for lack of coverage.<br /> <br /> Who is advocating for freedom for women here? And with who's view on the matter do you align with?<br /> <br /> Why is nudity the new taboo? Why is sex? Prostitution?<br /> <br /> If art depiction of women is a true concern of yours, try enacting positive change. Who are the artists drawing adequately? Contact them and have them submit work for Onyx Path. Contact Onyx Path art directors and tell them about these artists. Do something besides complaining!<br /> <br /> And while you're at it, don't forget to mention us guys too. I don't know about you, but I have been bombarded with unrealistic expectations of how I should look and dress my whole life.<br /> <br /> Who here has the physiques presented in men's art? Who has those manes of hair? Those bulges? Everyone is a armani decked body builder with a horse's mane and cock but me?<br /> <br /> I will wait to see a balding, soft-belly, skinny armed, weak chinned, pencil dicked hero. If you have one please feel free to post.<br /> <br /> How tiring would it be if everytime we see a drawing of an Adonis, Hercules or Apollo, some complained like that? How relevant the complaint would be?<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225298-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225313#post1225313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What <i>kinds</i> of films are those?<br /> <br /> \u200bLike, I've seen bits and pieces of The Birth of a Nation, and I've seen the entirety of 12 Years a Slave, and both films feature southern American white people doing very unpleasant things to black people, and yet the films are not equivalent in their framing and priorities and what they intend the audience to take away from it.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo are you talking about films that seem to be trying to empower the actual people who are assaulting children? Or what, what's going on, what is the context?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I can tell they are shock inducers. They do it because they can and they want to push the boundaries of that freedom. Honestly I see no other purpose in them. But I'm not a film academic or involved in the industry. To me they serve no purpose at all.<br /> <br /> They really push some crazy sexual murder nightmarish shit that I find hard to even describe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225298-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225313#post1225313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bHonestly, I think this is a bit of a false flag. I don't believe that anybody in the last couple of pages of that thread was saying anything to the effect of somebody not having a right to produce something, or calling for some kind of boycott, or any of the other usual arguments. Hell, as I recall, the person actually said that they liked the art style, and was just critical of it for still having that standard of depicting women.<br /> <br /> \u200bNobody has talked about total censorship until right here. It's a false dichotomy, and a scare tactic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the comment was sort of &quot;oh I'm tired of naked lady drawings, its kinda sexist, but they draw so great that they can draw naked ladies&quot;, implying that if it was a shitty artist there would be an issue, but since the artist is so good they get a pass.<br /> <br /> So people are kind of suggesting that people should refrain from producing art they want, unless it pleases said people.<br /> <br /> It is a shitty blackhole where all efforts at curbing speech end up being drawn to. All rules apply, unless I think they should not apply. The problem is, most likely someone you don't like will establish the rules, and then you're screwed.<br /> <br /> I say stop complaining about who is producing art and how they produce.<br /> <br /> Start promoting art you like. Or produce art you like yourself.<br /> <br /> Try to win us over with mind boggling art. Don't nag us to death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T11:12:24-07:00","id":1225366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225320#post1225320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, but the question we should ask ourselves is - <i>does repeatedly asking that question serve a useful purpose</i>?<br /> <br /> And I would argue it does! Images of sexualized women are <i>everywhere</i>. If you need one for your game, you don't need to specifically look in the thread for Exalted inspirational images. Hell, you don't even need to type in some humiliating search keyword Pinterest will no doubt silently judge you for, like &quot;sexy warrior cat woman&quot;, because &quot;sexy&quot; is treated <i>as the default</i>. If there is no constant pushback, images of half-naked women <i>will</i> consume the thread, purely because the likelihood of any piece of art being both technically proficient <i>and</i> going against the cultural default is a lot smaller than the likelihood of them just being technically proficient.<br /> <br /> And we haven't even touched on the question of consumer appeal, ie. good art that depicts a half-naked lady is probably going to be liked and shared by a lot more people than good art that depicts something with comparatively niche appeal, like a Chinese bureaucrat. Now, what this means is that even if we assume that the people who use these forums are saints who are always mindful of the implications of the things they share, they are going to to find a lot more of the former than the latter (because it is liked and shared by a lot more people, and as a consequence, it will float to the top of search results), and them being people with a functional set of eyes, the thought will inevitably cross their minds &quot;well yeah, I mean, this is a half-naked lady but holy shit it is also <i>really good art</i>, I'm sure that posting it <i>just this one time</i> is going to be fine&quot;. And then, before you even know it, the thread will once again be full of half-naked ladies even though everybody who participated <i>did</i> actively think through the implications of what they post. All it took was people thinking that good art deserves to be shared no matter the subject.<br /> <br /> (I know that this argument could be characterized as telling people that we have a moral imperative to bully those who like good art until they stop sharing it if we don't like the subject matter, but I'll have to ask you to read it a bit more charitably.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Images of sexualized women are everywhere?!<br /> <br /> Sexualized pictures of humans are everywhere!<br /> <br /> If I may, do you identify as male? If so, do you consider yourself an average male? If so, when was the last time you felt represented in superhero art?<br /> <br /> Who is the mainstream superhero who is not the picture perfect sex god? Who is the mainstream superhero without a six-pack, tree trunk legs, a mountanous back, jaw dropping arms and an italian salami in his pants? Who is this guy? <br /> <br /> Sex sells. Its old. Its vulgar. But it is an equal opportunity frustrator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T11:19:05-07:00","id":1225367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225358#post1225358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's worth reiterating that the comment that started this tangent had somebody saying that the art was amazing. If anything, the comment of not being a fan of scantily clad women read as a piece of context to the effect of it being something that looked so good that it got past a usual objection.<br /> <br /> \u200bUnless one was to think that my comment on the oversimplification of &quot;response to not liking something is as simple as not watching it&quot; was the insidious call for universal censorship?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying those are inadequate images for &quot;Exalted Inspiration&quot;? The thread asks for there to be no criticism of peoples taste in art. But people constantly criticize when it is art depicting women with little clothes.<br /> <br /> In that context my response was very simple.<br /> <br /> In that thread, please, if you don't like something, and that something is not against the terms of use, please don't look at it, don't take it as inspiration for your Exalted, and shut up about it!<br /> <br /> Its the polite thing to do!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T11:31:30-07:00","id":1225372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225348#post1225348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are there two threads for this?<br /> <br /> \u200bYou know, on a personal note, I'll also comment on how it's worth being critical of art depicting women in extremely skimpy clothes in fantasy just because it's a bit lazy.<br /> <br /> \u200bNot just in the sense of lacking variation and going to a very basic template, but on the most basic sense of &quot;doing less work&quot;; one has all the potential for unmoored creativity that fantasy permits, and instead opts to draw as little cloth as possible. A thin strip around the chest, a skirt with a slit in it and boots, and then done.<br /> <br /> \u200bBringing up Jen before was interesting, considering that on most of the occasions in which he draws women, he puts them in elaborately layered and patterned and folded clothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I thought theinternet had eaten my post creation, and posted twice, thats why I deleted the other one.<br /> <br /> I brought up Jen because he is a self proclaimed sexual person. Who produces sometimes sexualized art most people here enjoy. It's just that generally he sexualizes men, so that is alright.<br /> <br /> I like sexualized art of both males and females, Even though I'm a straight guy, who doesn't like looking at Chris Evans, Tyrese Gibson or whoever is the hunk of the hour?<br /> <br /> Why people complain about Hot and Flexible Djala Girl and not Jockstrap Sexgod Demonsword Guy?<br /> <br /> Its tiring. Be consistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T11:35:15-07:00","id":1225376,"title":"","content":"Oh God I remember why it's so difficult to handle discussions like this; deeply investing in them is exhausting, but avoiding them makes me feel like a coward.<br /> <br /> Keep it simple, keep it simple...<br /> <br /> \u200bThe manner in which actual women choose to dress is their own business, and there's something to be said for a particular style as representation. That would be a case in which I would still be critical of an oversaturation because of it obscuring styles as representation of particular people amidst a generic default.<br /> <br /> \u200bCriticism is not invalidated by the usual statement of &quot;if you don't like it, make something else&quot;, because the purpose of criticism is to analyse things. Negative criticism can become conflated with just stating hatred for something, but it doesn't have to be, it's fallacious to assume that it is, and when it is not it is a valid method of evaluating art.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe point about men is a false equivalence because the cultural context is not the same; I think that we're long past the criticism of oversexualized art as an unrealistic standard for women, because even that idea is evaluating primarily in terms of how the appearance of women is a commodity for others, which is not the point.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think it was fine to remind somebody of how that particular thread was not really a space for the criticism, and would have had no challenge for a comment requesting that it stay on focus. I do challenge the general sentiments of &quot;people being critical in this way is happening too often&quot; and &quot;having an objection to art is as simple as ignoring it&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T11:53:18-07:00","id":1225385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225366#post1225366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Images of sexualized women are everywhere?!<br /> <br /> Sexualized pictures of humans are everywhere!<br /> <br /> If I may, do you identify as male? If so, do you consider yourself an average male? If so, when was the last time you felt represented in superhero art?<br /> <br /> Who is the mainstream superhero who is not the picture perfect sex god? Who is the mainstream superhero without a six-pack, tree trunk legs, a mountanous back, jaw dropping arms and an italian salami in his pants? Who is this guy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think a good way to look at the discrepancy I'm trying to point out here is to go to a picture repository of your choice (I use Pinterest nowadays, but I'm sure there are alternatives), and search for something relatively innocuous like &quot;[insert gender] warrior&quot;.<br /> <br /> When searching for female warriors, it took me five pages to get flooded with an absolute deluge of swimsuit combatants such as <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/564x/a4/7b/f6/a47bf65f7123909b0a9b705c271339c4.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/564x/e4/53/46/e453462125261063373048b9ea3eb8b8.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> and <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/564x/75/00/c0/7500c006248a47eb2526bbdd82c9ddf3.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. On average, I got two such pictures per screen in the first five screens (Pinterest's weird layout means that you usually get more than six, but less than twelve images per screen, so let's call this a roughly 20% rate of images where characters are sexualized <i>to the point of excluding practicality</i>).<br /> <br /> To my surprise, when I entered &quot;male warrior&quot; into the search field, I also got quite a few images that featured bare-chested hunks. I had to exclude one for having realistic proportions (including belly fat - when was the last time you've seen a sexualized image of a warrior woman with <i>belly fat</i>?) and two more for having monstrous features (maws with gaping teeth) that seemed like clear signifiers that these characters were not meant to be seen as sexy. This left me with five guys in total, roughly half the number of sexualized women. (These five do, however, seem to fit the description you gave: <a href=\"https://hu.pinterest.com/pin/367747125818102410/\" target=\"_blank\">example number one</a>, <a href=\"https://hu.pinterest.com/pin/25966135337014547/\" target=\"_blank\">two</a>, <a href=\"https://hu.pinterest.com/pin/289285976060051603/\" target=\"_blank\">three</a>.)<br /> <br /> <br /> So apparently, even after meticulously taking the time to allow Pinterest's picture recommendation algorithms to get used to the idea that I generally won't click on, much less save images of scantily-clad women, I still got roughly twice as many hits of sexualized images with a search keyword that has no business giving me sexualized images when I was specifically looking for women than I got when I was looking for men. Sexualized pictures of both genders may exist, but there is definitely a discrepancy in how prominent they are!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T11:54:12-07:00","id":1225387,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> <br /> <br /> Yeah, we'll have to just disagree on this.<br /> <br /> I believe we're way past about caring for women or men, and should be on track about caring for people.<br /> <br /> Monolithic art portrayals are just as damaging for boys as they are for girls, but it is common for people not to think so. It is a relic of sexism that progressive people should be fighting to end, but strangely is dismissed most of the time.<br /> <br /> I grew up feeling completely inadequate, well into my twenties, even though I am very lucky looks wise. I was a male model in my late teens and early twenties and had body dysmorphia. I went from a 15 BMI to a 34 a couple of times before I was finally able to figure it out, by that time I was 28 years old. I lived in confusion and depression from around 9 to 27. <br /> <br /> It affected my family life, my socal life, my school life and my professional life.<br /> <br /> You think I'm alone?<br /> <br /> And I dare not ever speak of this, cause I'm a guy right? So we have it easy. We don't need help or for the people who fight for decent things to fight for decent things for us too. We will just figure or tough it out, since we're men, and we're so smart and strong.<br /> <br /> Yeah, ok. Got it. Very progressive and caring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T12:10:35-07:00","id":1225397,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3443_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3443\" data-vbnamecard=\"3443\">aluminiumtrioxid</a> <br /> <br /> What happens is that female warriors are by a innumerably vast majority a product of fantasy.<br /> <br /> For males, there are reality based comparisons.<br /> <br /> ANY man in most countries, TODAY, can still be drafted and made to be warriors. To sent to fight and die for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> The female warrior, is by her very nature, an idealized fantasy. For the longest time that wasn't, and still isn't, something that is expected of women.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But I asked you to look into a superhero. Who is the ideal male who is generally depicted in art? Who is the ideal woman? Are they that different? Is one less based in sexual fantasy than the other?<br /> <br /> And sex is seen as a &quot;female power&quot;. Women fought FOR this until last decade or so. We have &quot;PUSSY POWER&quot; we have &quot;SLUT WALKS&quot;. <br /> <br /> Super artists with so much girl power, Taylor Swift, Beyonc\u00e9, Lady Gaga. How do they dress when they want to project power? What do they present? Do you think they are victims? Do you think they are wrong?<br /> <br /> I don't know. Like Isator said, this discussion requires too much thought and emotional investment for it to be worth it most of the times, and I think I'm about reaching my limit...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T12:32:41-07:00","id":1225406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225397#post1225397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens is that female warriors are by a innumerably vast majority a product of fantasy.<br /> <br /> For males, there are reality based comparisons.<br /> <br /> ANY man in most countries, TODAY, can still be drafted and made to be warriors. To sent to fight and die for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> The female warrior, is by her very nature, an idealized fantasy. For the longest time that wasn't, and still isn't, something that is expected of women.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean - looking at the outfit of male warriors on a lot of these pictures, the amount of unnecessary and sometimes even counter-productive ornamentation, one could easily make the argument that the images of non-sexualized male warriors are no less rooted in fantasy than the sexualized ones. Yet the discrepancy remains, despite the fact that these male warrior figures also represent idealized fantasy versions of the real things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225397#post1225397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I asked you to look into a superhero. Who is the ideal male who is generally depicted in art? Who is the ideal woman? Are they that different? Is one less based in sexual fantasy than the other?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As for superheroes - male superheroes are depicted as attractive and powerful. Female ones as attractive. It should not be very difficult to draw superheroines with reasonable muscle mass who are, nevertheless, attractive. Yet it is not being done (exceptions notwithstanding - I recall some Wonder Woman art is pretty good in this respect). Again, a discrepancy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225397#post1225397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And sex is seen as a &quot;female power&quot;. Women fought FOR this until last decade or so. We have &quot;PUSSY POWER&quot; we have &quot;SLUT WALKS&quot;.<br /> <br /> Super artists with so much girl power, Taylor Swift, Beyonc\u00e9, Lady Gaga. How do they dress when they want to project power? What do they present? Do you think they are victims? Do you think they are wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A fantastic quote jumps to mind: &quot;Beauty is powerful because it is pleasing. Real power means not having to please.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225397#post1225397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know. Like Isator said, this discussion requires too much thought and emotional investment for it to be worth it most of the times, and I think I'm about reaching my limit...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is perfectly fine - the world is not going to spontaneously explode just because a stupid internet argument gets dropped halfway through. Take care of yourself, you don't have to do this if it is not fun. We can always just agree to disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T13:34:25-07:00","id":1225431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225406#post1225406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I mean - looking at the outfit of male warriors on a lot of these pictures, the amount of unnecessary and sometimes even counter-productive ornamentation, one could easily make the argument that the images of non-sexualized male warriors are no less rooted in fantasy than the sexualized ones. Yet the discrepancy remains, despite the fact that these male warrior figures also represent idealized fantasy versions of the real things.<br /> <br /> As for superheroes - male superheroes are depicted as attractive and powerful. Female ones as attractive. It should not be very difficult to draw superheroines with reasonable muscle mass who are, nevertheless, attractive. Yet it is not being done (exceptions notwithstanding - I recall some Wonder Woman art is pretty good in this respect). Again, a discrepancy.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>For both, warriors and superheros, I believe it traces back to what you see as attractive and what you see as powerful. You seem to be separating the 2 too much. The line between those things are very blurried and tenuous. You say superhero men are depcited as both &quot;attractive and powerful&quot; and women only as &quot;attractive&quot;. You're equating muscle mass with power, when for the idealized male muscle mass is just another attractiveness dial. To dissociate male muscle mass from attractiveness you have to tone it up to absurd, practically impossible proportions (Hulk), for it to start being a power factor.<br /> <br /> Until you reach that point, you're establishing a baseline look that is had by all who matter. Just like for women. So I disagree that there is this division here.<br /> <br /> I don't know if you want to discuss why men and women have diferent FFMI, and why &quot;general&quot; optimal attractiveness is at a different percentage for each sex.<br /> <br /> Women have naturally lower lean mass and need more fat to operate optimally. That is biological reality. At very low body fat women start having hormonal problems that result in temporary infertility.<br /> <br /> They are unable to naturally sustain the same proportions as a male without modern medicine and unhealthy side effects. Perception of health has been, with the exception of a few fads (ex: heroin chic) one of the best measures of attractiveness since forever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225406#post1225406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A fantastic quote jumps to mind: &quot;Beauty is powerful because it is pleasing. Real power means not having to please.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that quote is a bit contrived. Beauty has been power for both sexes for ages.<br /> <br /> Look at all the data at how all beautiful people, men and women, have major advantages in practically any endeavor they attempt. Its reality. Beauty is very powerful.<br /> <br /> Are you implying those women are powerless men pleasers? That their exploration of their sexiness is not real power, and no matter what they think, they're victims? Who do they have to please? Me? Because by what you're saying it seems like you think they have to please you and your standards to be considered powerful.<br /> <br /> What do they have to do or be to look &quot;really powerful&quot;? Beat Lincoln Hawk in arm wrestling and look like Rene Campbell or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 06-06-2018, 04:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T14:12:21-07:00","id":1225456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225431#post1225431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For both, warriors and superheros, I believe it traces back to what you see as attractive and what you see as powerful. You seem to be separating the 2 too much. The line between those things are very blurried and tenuous. You say superhero men are depcited as both &quot;attractive and powerful&quot; and women only as &quot;attractive&quot;. You're equating muscle mass with power, when for the idealized male muscle mass is just another attractiveness dial. To dissociate male muscle mass from attractiveness you have to tone it up to absurd, practically impossible proportions (Hulk), for it to start being a power factor.<br /> <br /> Until you reach that point, you're establishing a baseline look that is had by all who matter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As somebody who is very much attracted to men, I can safely tell you that this guy:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.el19digital.com/files/articulos/140608.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> could, in my book, easily lose something like 10-25% of his ridiculously exaggerated muscle mass without it impacting his attractiveness in any meaningful way.<br /> <br /> I don't seem to be alone in this assessment:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.shortpacked.com/comics/2011-12-02-sexy.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Muscle mass definitely does hit diminishing returns on the attractiveness scale after a point. Male superheroes are usually depicted way, way beyond that point - this seems to signify that the exaggerated proportions are meant to signify <i>power</i>, not some sort of fuzzy &quot;baseline attractiveness&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> (I'll address the rest of your post at a later date, I have an exam coming up at Friday, so posts that require constructing a nuanced argument about the nature of power are somewhat beyond my ability to produce right now.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 06-06-2018, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T14:24:18-07:00","id":1225461,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">later on now</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T14:53:20-07:00","id":1225468,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3443_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3443\" data-vbnamecard=\"3443\">aluminiumtrioxid</a><br /> <br /> I agree with you completely. My wife says that all the time. She hates body-builder type physiques. We actually get into arguments, because I'm constantly trying to be &quot;fitter&quot;, and she says she likes more when I'm at what i would consider 10-20 lbs overweight (yeah right, amirite?).<br /> <br /> As a man who is totally attracted to women I can safely say that most of the women depicted in the problematic way you're arguing against could be have 50% more coverage, have all their sliders dragged closer to the middle and still be, or be even more extremely beautiful head turners.<br /> <br /> And?<br /> <br /> Does reality matter? Aren't we talking about unreal depictions causing distorted expectations?<br /> <br /> Do you think that boys that read Batman, Superman, Aquaman, The Flash, have this perception? That is baseline ideal. To be anyone that matters, thats how you look. Was there a time when one of those guys got told by a crush, they looked too buff? Did the girl ever look at a more realistic man with longing in a comic? Hell, did they ever lose the girl to some normal guy?<br /> <br /> Even Peter Parker, nerd hero supreme, only gets Mary Jane after he becomes the shredded beast Spiderman.<br /> <br /> I don't if I'm reading or understanding something wrong here, but I see this last post of yours as arguing the same as me.<br /> <br /> The exact same shit happens to both sexes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a><br /> <br /> Ah, I didn't now we had to wait for everything on the Ever Unfurling Scroll of Grievances to be checked before we started arguing for what is right. But ok, I guess doing good things will have to wait until thats done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 06-06-2018, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T15:08:15-07:00","id":1225477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225468#post1225468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with you completely. My wife says that all the time. She hates body-builder type physiques. We actually get into arguments, because I'm constantly trying to be &quot;fitter&quot;, and she says she likes more when I'm at what i would consider 10-20 lbs overweight (yeah right, amirite?).<br /> <br /> As a man who is totally attracted to women I can safely say that most of the women depicted in the problematic way you're arguing against could be have 50% more coverage, have all their sliders dragged closer to the middle and still be, or be even more extremely beautiful head turners.<br /> <br /> And?<br /> <br /> Does reality matter? Aren't we talking about unreal depictions causing distorted expectations?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well... no? I'm specifically trying to support the claim that there is a discrepancy between how male and female superheroes are portrayed, with the first group's portrayal primarily being aimed at depicting strength (as evidenced by the fact that they are more muscular than a purely attractiveness-based approach would warrant), and the second group's portrayal... not really having that goal.<br /> <br /> (Which is not to say that the images of idealized male bodies we're inundated with can't fuck somebody's self-image up just as effectively no matter what the artist was meant to convey, but I made a specific claim, you contested that claim, so I brought up an example in support of it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T15:08:19-07:00","id":1225478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225468#post1225468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, I didn't now we had to wait for everything on the Ever Unfurling Scroll of Grievances to be checked before we started arguing for what is right. But ok, I guess doing good things will have to wait until thats done.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand this.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'll admit, when you started bringing in personal issues, I both hesitated and felt an impulse towards responses that would have been insensitive. I'm sorry about that.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut I do think that the image of machismo that you're talking about having been hurt by is not something created for the benefit of women. Patriarchy hurts men too; it hurts them when they don't live up to its standards, it hurts them when they act in defiance of it, and it hurts them when it compels behaviour that just alienates them from others.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd I probably do argue about that less than I do the other side; not because I think it's all right, but as something that has stood out less to me personally, and where the other side is something that I feel a need to make up a lot for.<br /> <br /> What you've expressed is giving me a sense for how I might improve upon that.<br /> <br /> \u200bI do find myself feeling as though Jen's depictions of men don't fall into the trap of problematic machismo very much due to coupling their physiques with a sense of emotional sensitivity and honesty that is uncommonly coupled with that image.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T15:32:42-07:00","id":1225483,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3443_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3443\" data-vbnamecard=\"3443\">aluminiumtrioxid</a> <br /> <br /> Ah, I'm starting to have a realization... I think that in believing I found common ground with you, I understood where we are misunderstanding each other.<br /> <br /> You're saying that all this serves male power fantasies, that originate, obviously, in males. So males are the &quot;abusers&quot; here.<br /> <br /> I don't dispute that. I agree. Let me just add that what you see that as &quot;power&quot; decoupled from sex (attractiveness), that fat bald dude in the comic sees it as &quot;power to be the most sexiest to get all the girls&quot;. He is clueless as to what females actually want, and he inflicts that cluelessness on the masses of kids. The greatest power of all is to get the girl. Don't for a minute forget that.<br /> <br /> Batman does not have impossible forearms because he needs those to justify his strength. He has impossible forearms because fat bald guy thinks women love that, and Batman needs to have those so that he looks boss for Catwoman.<br /> <br /> So all that muscle is his misguided attempt at making the most attractive guy ever. Real &quot;power&quot; fantasies are actually decoupled from physical equivalence, they are more magical, reality-bending, Superman is stronger than the Hulk, even though the Hulk is bigger. Because Superman is special, he has the power of the sun. That is power fantasy.<br /> <br /> Looks are just peacocks fanning their tails, its for one reason only. Don't think that because they're failing at being attractive to females that they are not trying to do that.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying boys suffer as much as girls from this agression. I'm asking people to raise their standard for all victims not only half of them. If you're asking for less unrealistic and sexualized art depictions, please do so when you encounter that for males too. Its just consistent and decent.<br /> <br /> In essence we don't disagree that much, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T15:57:49-07:00","id":1225486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225478#post1225478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't understand this.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'll admit, when you started bringing in personal issues, I both hesitated and felt an impulse towards responses that would have been insensitive. I'm sorry about that.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut I do think that the image of machismo that you're talking about having been hurt by is not something created for the benefit of women. Patriarchy hurts men too; it hurts them when they don't live up to its standards, it hurts them when they act in defiance of it, and it hurts them when it compels behaviour that just alienates them from others.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd I probably do argue about that less than I do the other side; not because I think it's all right, but as something that has stood out less to me personally, and where the other side is something that I feel a need to make up a lot for.<br /> <br /> What you've expressed is giving me a sense for how I might improve upon that.<br /> <br /> \u200bI do find myself feeling as though Jen's depictions of men don't fall into the trap of problematic machismo very much due to coupling their physiques with a sense of emotional sensitivity and honesty that is uncommonly coupled with that image.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the snark, I responded to that before you changed your post.<br /> <br /> And I'm sorry for turning this personal and unloading this here but, I was always the leftist progressive guy on my group. Latin America brims with machismo and conservative. I was always the one who spoke in defense and extended the hand for the LGBTQ people, for the socially awkward, for the less financially fortunate.<br /> <br /> I embraced Equality, I thought we were this big umbrella, that we would all hug each other and demolish the oppressors to create a society that is sensible to the individual.<br /> <br /> But as a hetero male recently, I just feel completely excluded. If I say a certain issue affects guys too and we should make this argument genderless, people immediately dismiss it. <br /> <br /> They scream &quot;The Patriarchy is the Problem!&quot; &quot;You are a man!&quot; &quot;You don't suffer!&quot;<br /> <br /> What the hell?<br /> <br /> This shit does get personal. Yes I suffered. Greatly. Whats going on?<br /> <br /> Who cares if the abuse is male generated? I'm arguing for the victims here. I'm not saying guys are depicted as super muscular in comics because girls like that. <br /> <br /> Thing is boys' issues get immediately shutdown in any discussion for positive change. I fear for my son. I don't want him to suffer like I did. I want the change to happen for him as much as for my daughter.<br /> <br /> I'm already over my hang ups, I'm 35 and fairly successful, fairly satisfied with myself.<br /> <br /> But do I have to wait for everything to be perfect for women so that I argue for a better place for everyone?<br /> <br /> Do I raise my son to be as Patriarcly Succesful as possible, because by the time we get to his issues he will be an old man? I'm seriously considering this, and maybe even unconsiously doing it already... I dunno.<br /> <br /> I would be more amneable to say that we need to take more care of female depictions right now. But on a sample, when was the depiction of men in fantasy ever questioned in that thread? How about women?<br /> <br /> The disparity is staggering. It doesn't even get mentioned. And when it does it is either, mocked, dismissed or vilified.<br /> <br /> I'm getting repetitive here. Will leave for a bit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T19:31:22-07:00","id":1225511,"title":"","content":"I have a friend who's an artist. He frequently draws sexy women with little to no clothing. Why? Because he <i>enjoys</i> drawing sexy women who don't wear a lot of clothing. It's pretty much that simple really. Given the freedom when he can draw whatever he wants, 9 times out of 10 when he's drawing a picture for fun (rather than a commission or for his job) and I peek over to see what he's drawing - yup, it's a sexy woman without a whole lot of clothing. He doesn't draw those pictures because he's particularly sexist, and he's not thinking about any kind of larger cultural issues. He just draws what he likes.<br /> <br /> I think this is an issue with the way women (and men) are frequently portrayed in drawings. They tend to be idealized versions in which the artist is drawing something they think looks cool, or sexy, or what have you. Probably because, at the end of the day, many artists enjoy drawing half-naked sexy men and women more than they enjoy drawing half-naked obese balding people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-06-2018, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T23:32:32-07:00","id":1225526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225468#post1225468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The exact same shit happens to both sexes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simply put, this will never not be this. Men and women are different, the expectations they have are different and the beauty standards, while having communal roots that don't really change with time, are still also different.<br /> <br /> You can, of course, dig as many exceptions as you want, those don't matter to talk about the norm.<br /> And the norm will always have some discrepancy or another when comparing between sexes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225511#post1225511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a friend who's an artist. He frequently draws sexy women with little to no clothing. Why? Because he <i>enjoys</i> drawing sexy women who don't wear a lot of clothing. It's pretty much that simple really. Given the freedom when he can draw whatever he wants, 9 times out of 10 when he's drawing a picture for fun (rather than a commission or for his job) and I peek over to see what he's drawing - yup, it's a sexy woman without a whole lot of clothing. He doesn't draw those pictures because he's particularly sexist, and he's not thinking about any kind of larger cultural issues. He just draws what he likes.<br /> <br /> I think this is an issue with the way women (and men) are frequently portrayed in drawings. They tend to be idealized versions in which the artist is drawing something they think looks cool, or sexy, or what have you. Probably because, at the end of the day, many artists enjoy drawing half-naked sexy men and women more than they enjoy drawing half-naked obese balding people.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Pretty much. And that's fine. If people feel bothered because one gendered depiction is unpleasingly trended, they can look at the other side. Tumblr, for example, is overwhelmingly populated by women. There you will see things drawn in a skewed female perspective, exactly like some other media (say, deviantart) will show a skewed male perspective. That demography even happened spontaneously, and UX professionals suffer to discover why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 06-07-2018, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T05:56:51-07:00","id":1225552,"title":"","content":"A couple of issues are getting mixed here.<br /> <br /> 1) Problematic portrayal of women in art, let's take rpg's and comics for now. Now, for me it's not lack of clothes, or that those girls sexy. I can quite enjoy that, I assure you, and I am hardly the only woman to do so. What makes it problematic, for me at least, is that they are purely drawn as eye candy. The bad art doesn't depict protagonists, they are not power fantasies and I can't identify with them, it's just fan service aimed at men. Too many of those is a clear flag that this space is not meant for women. The guys, even when sexy and bare-chested and whatnot, they're not like that, even remotely. Usually they're depicting doing something heroic and saving the day. <i>That</i> is the difference, and you'll of course see this difference in depiction of men and women in a lot of places.<br /> <br /> 2) Idealization of an almost unattainable beauty ideal. Yes, you men also suffer from that. Nobody will ever argue about that.<br /> <br /> 3) And that leads us to 'Whataboutism'. The two issues described above are separate, and addressing one does not imply <i>anything </i>about the other. Both are bad, and one existing does not excuse the existence of the other and vice versa. But bringing up the second to dismiss or minimize the first is bad form. That this is a standard derailing tactic of the (alt-)right, MRA, red-pillers and their ilk also <i>really </i>does not help. Not implying that someone here is posting with such an agenda, but been in enough such debates where it was used to have become particularly allergic to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T08:13:44-07:00","id":1225583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225552#post1225552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple of issues are getting mixed here.<br /> <br /> 1) Problematic portrayal of women in art, let's take rpg's and comics for now. Now, for me it's not lack of clothes, or that those girls sexy. I can quite enjoy that, I assure you, and I am hardly the only woman to do so. What makes it problematic, for me at least, is that they are purely drawn as eye candy. The bad art doesn't depict protagonists, they are not power fantasies and I can't identify with them, it's just fan service aimed at men. Too many of those is a clear flag that this space is not meant for women. The guys, even when sexy and bare-chested and whatnot, they're not like that, even remotely. Usually they're depicting doing something heroic and saving the day. <i>That</i> is the difference, and you'll of course see this difference in depiction of men and women in a lot of places.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are separating your two issues clearly, and that is awesome. Other people didn't. They actually seem to have a different issue than you, or didn't articulate as clearly as you, and that is what I was arguing with. You have won me 100% on the this.<br /> <br /> So why all the complain about lack of clothing?<br /> <br /> And no complaining about the actual issue?<br /> <br /> Yes! Lets have more heroic female characters doing more heroic shit (naked or not), and less of them lounging around looking hot and bothered (I say less, not none, I like art of heroic hot and bothered people lounging around <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)!<br /> <br /> I'll stand side by side with you on this one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225552#post1225552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Idealization of an almost unattainable beauty ideal. Yes, you men also suffer from that. Nobody will ever argue about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not as simple as not saying people don't argue that. It is very common to dismiss any kind of men suffering. It is extremely sexist.<br /> <br /> Even the comic posted to explain the issue has a sexist beauty standard.<br /> <br /> Why is the clueless artist fat and bald? Because those things make it easier for the viewer to not like him, and therefore dismiss his idea (however wrong that idea may be). And fat bald losers are the nerds who draw comics right? So many damaging stereotypes it boggles the mind<br /> <br /> And then she goes on to draw a sexually objectified Batman, just that this time he is sexually objectified for women, so presumably thats fine.<br /> <br /> She started right talking about form and function and then went on to chiseled jaw lines, nice eyes and pouty lips. Instead of explaining that different women find different things attractive and Batman should be drawn as an Athlete and Martial Artist, and whatever else doesn't have a right way to do?<br /> <br /> Please reverse the gender identities on this one and tell me how this looks.<br /> <br /> A cute guy telling a fat woman with bad hair to stop drawing super voluptuous vixens and start drawing athletic women with feline eyes, angelic faces and full lips, because that is what guys actually like.<br /> <br /> Seriously? False-equivalency? Give me a break. I'm so used to this that I'm tired of it.<br /> <br /> And the vast majority of people interested in body acceptance issues wouldn't even blink at it. Because the target is the Patriarchy. And boys and men's issues are just collateral in the war.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225552#post1225552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) And that leads us to 'Whataboutism'. The two issues described above are separate, and addressing one does not imply <i>anything </i>about the other. Both are bad, and one existing does not excuse the existence of the other and vice versa. But bringing up the second to dismiss or minimize the first is bad form. That this is a standard derailing tactic of the (alt-)right, MRA, red-pillers and their ilk also <i>really </i>does not help. Not implying that someone here is posting with such an agenda, but been in enough such debates where it was used to have become particularly allergic to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't do any &quot;whataboutism&quot; here. I only said that if the person has issues with sexually objectifying art, and they were going to act upon it, to also please consider that this issue also affect boys, and include them in their activism. And that act, bringing boys issues, as always gets unwarranted pushback.<br /> <br /> I don't care to trade misogyny for misandry. I want to get Equality. I don't think we need to wait for anything to be even to start moving to a place where everyone is well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 06-07-2018, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T08:26:11-07:00","id":1225589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225526#post1225526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply put, this will never not be this. Men and women are different, the expectations they have are different and the beauty standards, while having communal roots that don't really change with time, are still also different.<br /> <br /> You can, of course, dig as many exceptions as you want, those don't matter to talk about the norm.<br /> And the norm will always have some discrepancy or another when comparing between sexes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry Synapse, I don't get if you're nit-picking my use of &quot;exact same&quot; or if you don't agree that beauty standards affect men, or that they don't affect enough men (or men enough) to matter discussing, or what.<br /> <br /> I will clarify that &quot;exact same&quot; was a manner of expression, and I do understand men and women are different in many ways (thankfully).<br /> <br /> If you would like to discuss this further, can you clarify?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 06-07-2018, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T08:42:00-07:00","id":1225594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225583#post1225583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">I didn't do any &quot;whataboutism&quot; here. I only said that if the person has issues with sexually objectifying art, and they were going to act upon it, to also please consider that this issue also affect boys, and include them in their activism. And that act, bringing boys issues, as always gets unwarranted pushback.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">That is literally the definition of whataboutism...</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Someone says sexually objectifying women in art is bad, and you say 'well its bad when men are objectified too'.<br /> <br /> If you want to complain about art that objectifies men, do it when a piece of art that objectifies men is shown not when one that shows women is.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":".  Fixed those errant COLOR tags 06-07-2018, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T08:50:10-07:00","id":1225599,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1329_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1329\" data-vbnamecard=\"1329\">ElvesofZion</a><br /> <br /> No, that would be if I used the fact that men also get sexually objectified in art to dismiss their concern that women get sexually obejctified in art.<br /> <br /> I didn't do that.<br /> <br /> I asked that if they were going to work on this real issue, to not forget that men suffer from that too, and to include us in their concern and work.<br /> <br /> I'm not dismissing anything here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T08:57:21-07:00","id":1225601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225599#post1225599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1329_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1329\" data-vbnamecard=\"1329\">ElvesofZion</a><br /> <br /> No, that would be if I used the fact that men also get sexually objectified in art to dismiss their concern that women get sexually obejctified in art.<br /> <br /> I didn't do that.<br /> <br /> I asked that if they were going to work on this real issue, to not forget that men suffer from that too, and to include us in their concern and work.<br /> <br /> I'm not dismissing anything here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You think anyone who is dismissing it calls out that they are doing so? The whole point of whataboutism is that it casually dismiss the point by suggesting that this other thing should be talked about instead/as much/as well.<br /> <br /> There are lots of issues that need to be addressed in society, I won't argue that. But we should let them each breath in their own space. <br /> <br /> You may not be intentionally dismissing the issue, but you are deflecting from it none the less by bringing up how 'men are objectified too'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T09:08:52-07:00","id":1225603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225583#post1225583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its not as simple as not saying people don't argue that. It is very common to dismiss any kind of men suffering. It is extremely sexist.<br /> <br /> Even the comic posted to explain the issue has a sexist beauty standard.<br /> <br /> Why is the clueless artist fat and bald? Because those things make it easier for the viewer to not like him, and therefore dismiss his idea (however wrong that idea may be). And fat bald losers are the nerds who draw comics right? So many damaging stereotypes it boggles the mind<br /> <br /> And then she goes on to draw a sexually objectified Batman, just that this time he is sexually objectified for women, so presumably thats fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of that comic was that objectifying <i>both</i> men and women is undesirable. The woman is obviously uncomfortable with, gives the guy an example of the reverse and he is now uncomfortable. I honestly can not see how you would come to the conclusion that the message of that comic is that when it's men it's ok?<br /> <br /> Also, that guy is normal looking, just like the geeky girl with glasses is. You are projecting a great deal here, in my humble opinion. Check out that artist's comics before making such assumptions. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225583#post1225583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the vast majority of people interested in body acceptance issues wouldn't even blink at it. Because the target is the Patriarchy. And boys and men's issues are just collateral in the war.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope you see that being sexually objectifying women happens a great deal more than sexually objectifying men? As in orders of magnitudes? The 'male gaze' is omni-present, the 'female gaze'? Not so much. And that objectifying women was the topic at hand? Not body acceptance? <br /> <br /> Nobody here was dismissing men, so please don't make it about that. I'm sure people would be more than pleased to discuss men's issues as well. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225583#post1225583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't do any &quot;whataboutism&quot; here. I only said that if the person has issues with sexually objectifying art, and they were going to act upon it, to also please consider that this issue also affect boys, and include them in their activism. And that act, bringing boys issues, as always gets unwarranted pushback.<br /> <br /> I don't care to trade misogyny for misandry. I want to get Equality. I don't think we need to wait for anything to be even to start moving to a place where everyone is well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I'll be blunt: yes, you were, and obviously you still are! Feminist activism does <i>not </i>need to include men's rights. And that does not equal a false equivalence or misandry, nor does it mean that men's issues are just collateral in some war, nor is it sexist, nor is it an attack on equality. Honestly, we were discussing sexual objectification in rpg's and comics here, an issue that almost overwhelmingly affects women, so yes, <i>of course </i>you can expect pushback if you argue that men are equally victimized. The sexism inherent in our society is toxic for all parties involved, and creates issues for all genders, but they are <i>different</i>. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T10:15:10-07:00","id":1225614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225583#post1225583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the comic posted to explain the issue has a sexist beauty standard.<br /> <br /> Why is the clueless artist fat and bald? Because those things make it easier for the viewer to not like him, and therefore dismiss his idea (however wrong that idea may be). And fat bald losers are the nerds who draw comics right? So many damaging stereotypes it boggles the mind</div> </div> </div> </div>He's not an artist, he's a guy who comes into the store to complain about females getting represented as characters. From his character write-up, 'Arch is very concerned about gender inequality and misrepresentation in popular media. Specifically, he's concerned that other people might be talking about it, thereby using up valuable time that could be spent discussing dude problems.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And then she goes on to draw a sexually objectified Batman, just that this time he is sexually objectified for women, so presumably thats fine. </div> </div> </div>She's explaining that the sexual fantasy is an objectifying one. That when artists draw only scantily clad and sexy women, they're just representing them as sex objects, things for people who like women to get off with, with nothing more. Characters like Batman and Superman are power fantasies, they represent what you could be, they are not objects for your desire, but aspirations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T10:56:46-07:00","id":1225627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225603#post1225603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The point of that comic was that objectifying <i>both</i> men and women is undesirable. The woman is obviously uncomfortable with, gives the guy an example of the reverse and he is now uncomfortable. I honestly can not see how you would come to the conclusion that the message of that comic is that when it's men it's ok?<br /> <br /> Also, that guy is normal looking, just like the geeky girl with glasses is. You are projecting a great deal here, in my humble opinion. Check out that artist's comics before making such assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Its so innocent portraying the bad guy in an unnattractive way. Its one of the oldest tricks in the book. <br /> <br /> Are you being deliberately obtuse in trying to say that man and that girl are on the same scale of what the mainstream considers attractive? It borders on the malicious.<br /> <br /> I had a reaction to that specific strip, if a piece shouldn't be appreciate as a single piece then it shouldn't be offered as such. I'm not interested in it to look at it further.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225603#post1225603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope you see that being sexually objectifying women happens a great deal more than sexually objectifying men? As in orders of magnitudes? The 'male gaze' is omni-present, the 'female gaze'? Not so much. And that objectifying women was the topic at hand? Not body acceptance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we shifting the conversation out of hero art to in general now? Because if we're staying on topic, no I don't agree with you. Hero art sexually objectifies both genders to a degree of negligible difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225603#post1225603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody here was dismissing men, so please don't make it about that. I'm sure people would be more than pleased to discuss men's issues as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>So why does it turn to a shitstorm when men are mentioned?<br /> <br /> My general stance on this, remains the same. Don't like it, don't consume it. If you're interested in working to change it, it would be nice if you consider the other half of the population too. But knock yourself out if you don't want to, its your time. Just not gonna win me over, not that it matters any or you should care.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225603#post1225603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I'll be blunt: yes, you were, and obviously you still are! Feminist activism does <i>not </i>need to include men's rights. And that does not equal a false equivalence or misandry, nor does it mean that men's issues are just collateral in some war, nor is it sexist, nor is it an attack on equality. Honestly, we were discussing sexual objectification in rpg's and comics here, an issue that almost overwhelmingly affects women, so yes, <i>of course </i>you can expect pushback if you argue that men are equally victimized. The sexism inherent in our society is toxic for all parties involved, and creates issues for all genders, but they are <i>different</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if it isn't a lie that feminism is about equality, then sorry, yes it does have to include men's rights. Specific activists or activities could focus on specific issues, but if feminism is about equality, in general, it has to act on issues of men and women.<br /> <br /> If you think sexual objectification in RPGs and Comics affects mostly women you are extremely blind to what is happening to boys and men, which is expected. The majority of the industry's consumers are male and it affects them greatly.<br /> <br /> There are hideous ramifications of this, with steroid abuse, oil injections, mental illness, suicide... Have you ever seen interviews with these guys that inject oil in themselves? They are asked if they believe women like the way they look, and baffingly say that yes, even when confronted with hordes of women telling them they don't like it, they don't seem to understand.<br /> <br /> These young men are being, sometimes irrepareably, damaged by this group of factors. This is overwhelmingly a men's issue too. Your blindness and dismissal of it is sad, and extremely common.<br /> <br /> But, bright side is, that while you ignored our agreement. I don't. <br /> <br /> Didn't you say you don't mind scantily clad sexy people in this type of art? Neither do I. And you have my support if you ever need it in arguing for more active roles for females in that type of art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T11:01:26-07:00","id":1225628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225601#post1225601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You think anyone who is dismissing it calls out that they are doing so? The whole point of whataboutism is that it casually dismiss the point by suggesting that this other thing should be talked about instead/as much/as well.<br /> <br /> There are lots of issues that need to be addressed in society, I won't argue that. But we should let them each breath in their own space.<br /> <br /> You may not be intentionally dismissing the issue, but you are deflecting from it none the less by bringing up how 'men are objectified too'.</div> </div> </div> </div>You: I need an apple.<br /> <br /> Me: You can get one at the corner store. By the way, I need one too, if you don't mind, get me one while you're there!<br /> <br /> You: WHY ARE YOU DISMISSING MY NEED FOR AN APPLE SAYING YOU NEED ONE TOO?!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T11:08:58-07:00","id":1225633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225614#post1225614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He's not an artist, he's a guy who comes into the store to complain about females getting represented as characters. From his character write-up, 'Arch is very concerned about gender inequality and misrepresentation in popular media. Specifically, he's concerned that other people might be talking about it, thereby using up valuable time that could be spent discussing dude problems.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! Good to know. Thank you for confirming that fat bald guy is the de facto bad guy. As was incredibly obvious. For a moment I thought I was projecting (Not!).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225614#post1225614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She's explaining that the sexual fantasy is an objectifying one. That when artists draw only scantily clad and sexy women, they're just representing them as sex objects, things for people who like women to get off with, with nothing more. Characters like Batman and Superman are power fantasies, they represent what you could be, they are not objects for your desire, but aspirations.</div> </div> </div> </div>So that makes Batman\u2019s and Superman\u2019s sexual objectification any less damaging?<br /> <br /> Because they\u2019re aspirations?<br /> <br /> That\u2019s the whole of the problem. They are unattainable aspirations that distort what a healthy body image should be, to incredibly damaging levels among boys and young men.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T11:21:38-07:00","id":1225635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225633#post1225633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that makes Batman\u2019s and Superman\u2019s sexual objectification any less damaging?<br /> <br /> Because they\u2019re aspirations?</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes it not sexual objectification. They aren't being portrayed as sex objects, they're being portrayed as ideals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That\u2019s the whole of the problem. They are unattainable aspirations that distort what a healthy body image should be, to incredibly damaging levels among boys and young men. </div> </div> </div>Eh, I think the overuse of these body types isn't helpful, but I don't know if there's any evidence of damage caused by them (would certainly be worth checking out).<br /> <br /> But you're either missing or sidestepping the problem. What these things are portraying to the readers, mostly males, is men being strong and confident, and women being sexually available.<br /> <br /> And in regards to 'whataboutism,' societal problems aren't really comparable to an apple you can just get across the street.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://chainsawsuit.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/12/20141204-patreon.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Here you see the problem better. Someone has an issue, it's an urgent issue that, if not solved, is going to go badly. When attention is brought to this issue, their issue is put to the side in the name of 'everyone's issues.' Dragging attention away from their issue, in the end doesn't solve any issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-07-2018, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T11:49:59-07:00","id":1225642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225635#post1225635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It makes it not sexual objectification. They aren't being portrayed as sex objects, they're being portrayed as ideals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, by your account, all the women are available to sleep with them. How are they not also sexually objecdtified?<br /> <br /> All these years doing it, and I never realized sex is a one way street. Who would\u2019ve known?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225635#post1225635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I think the overuse of these body types isn't helpful, but I don't know if there's any evidence of damage caused by them (would certainly be worth checking out).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. I\u2019ll let you re read all the literature produced by your allies, asking for women to be portrayed as something other than voluptuous vixens, and how damaging only having women portrayed as that is.<br /> <br /> And then please go argue your point with them. When you get them to accept what you\u2019re saying, please show me the way to the discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225635#post1225635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you're either missing or sidestepping the problem. What these things are portraying to the readers, mostly males, is men being strong and confident, and women being sexually available.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I addressed this above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225635#post1225635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in regards to 'whataboutism,' societal problems aren't really comparable to an apple you can just get across the street.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s a simplification to illustrate a point. You want me to explain to you how it relates? My guess is you\u2019re more than smart enough to have understood it.<br /> <br /> Are you not sure as to how to rebut the idea? Or you really think we should be discussing apples and corner stores?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225635#post1225635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here you see the problem better. Someone has an issue, it's an urgent issue that, if not solved, is going to go badly. When attention is brought to this issue, their issue is put to the side in the name of 'everyone's issues.' Dragging attention away from their issue, in the end doesn't solve any issues.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That you fail to see both houses are on fire, and the other one has been burning for a very long time is kinda sad. That you vilify me for asking for some of your water, too. (Or I could say that sexual objectification has nothing to do with fire trucks! Now about those firemen\u2026)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T11:56:41-07:00","id":1225646,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day, some material is designed to appeal to certain demographics over others. Content producers do this because they want to make money, and believe that demographic A will get offer more money for the content than demographic B will. As such they may include certain images or ideas that appeal to Demographic A but which Demographic B does not care for. That isn't necessarily a bad thing, in and of itself. In fact, I think it would be problematic to demand that content producers set out from the get-go to produce content that is inoffensive to Demographics A, B, C, D and everyone else.<br /> <br /> Ultimately I am very much a member of the, &quot;If you don't like something vote with your wallet and don't buy it,&quot; school of thought, especially when it comes to artwork, writing and other forms of personal, highly creative content.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* Well I think that the greater point of this thread is going to end up getting lost anyway so whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-07-2018, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T11:57:13-07:00","id":1225647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225642#post1225642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, by your account, all the women are available to sleep with them. How are they not also sexually objecdtified?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they're free to do whatever they want, while the women are just portrayed as sexual objects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All these years doing it, and I never realized sex is a one way street. Who would\u2019ve known? </div> </div> </div>Hah, you're being glib. That's great, you know this is fictional representation, but it's still fiction that informs a lot of attitudes people have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok. I\u2019ll let you re read all the literature produced by your allies, asking for women to be portrayed as something other than voluptuous vixens, and how damaging only having women portrayed as that is. </div> </div> </div>My allies?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It\u2019s a simplification to illustrate a point. You want me to explain to you how it relates? My guess is you\u2019re more than smart enough to have understood it. </div> </div> </div>It's an oversimplification, and the 'go get me an apple while you're at it' is dismissive. By demanding a sharing of a focus, when one problem is not as bad as another, the more pressing problem is not getting the attention it deserves. This is especially important when it comes to government or societal reform, where attention is a primary currency.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are you not sure as to how to rebut the idea? Or you really think we should be discussing apples and corner stores?<br /> <br /> That you fail to see both houses are on fire, and the other one has been burning for a very long time is kinda sad. That you vilify me for asking for some of your water, too. (Or I could say that sexual objectification has nothing to do with fire trucks! Now about those firemen\u2026) </div> </div> </div>No one's villifying you. This is the 'whataboutism.' Saying women shouldn't be portrayed as sex objects isn't the same as saying you're a bad person.<br /> <br /> That said, your argument's a bit scattershot. Artists who choose to objectify people sexually, or choose not to, aren't forced into either stance by the government, but depending on the artist some might be reliant on their customer base.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-07-2018, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T12:23:49-07:00","id":1225656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225642#post1225642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That you fail to see both houses are on fire, and the other one has been burning for a very long time is kinda sad. That you vilify me for asking for some of your water, too. (Or I could say that sexual objectification has nothing to do with fire trucks! Now about those firemen\u2026)</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that both houses aren't on fire, the one house (sexually objectifying women) is on fire (the picture was posted), and all houses have a chance of being on fire (both men and women have negative portrayals in media), some more than others (women more so than men), and to different degrees (objectifying of women has been historically worse than that of men and is portrayed as passive and always sexual versus active and aspirational, even if unrealistically so). So when one person says my house is on fire, and that happens quite often and is prone to happen, saying my house also sometimes catches fire is 'whataboutism'.<br /> <br /> Nobody is saying that you can't advocate for better representation of male bodies in media, just do it when its the topic at hand rather than jumping in when someone is talking about a different thing in need of advocacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T12:27:55-07:00","id":1225659,"title":"","content":"Wow. Just wow <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> No, the guy in the comic is not the bad guy. That comic is just about <i>impossible</i> to misread. He is just engaging in whataboutism, Just like you. You <i>are </i>that guy. He is also depicted in a manner you want men to be depicted. Average. He is not an Adonis, no, but he's not a hideous abomination either! He's just... average. And here you are, drawing away attention from that comic's message from how women are objectified to something which clearly is not there, yet another example of whataboutism. Yes, someone is indeed arguing in bad faith!<br /> <br /> You also ignore the by now many arguments about how sexually objectifying of women is not the same as the power fantasies of men. Batman is depicted that way by men for men, and if you wish to argue that is done in a way to make the readers want to have sex him him, allow me to laugh in your face. <i>It is not the same! </i>Unattainable aspirations that distort what a healthy body image should be is something else entirely. You wish to talk about that, dedicate another thread to it and do not entangle it with what is clearly a women's issue.<br /> <br /> This is not me dismissing that issue, nor me being blind to them. This is me <i>separating</i> them. After all, it's not as if women do not struggle with unattainable beauty ideals. But that's not the problem of being reduced to sex objects.<br /> <br /> And in regard to how feminism should also advocate men's rights, or it's not about equality. Also laughable. That is not how emancipation works. I suppose BLM should be advocating for white people too and those who fight poverty for the rights of the 1%'s. Yeah right.<br /> <br /> So could we please spin the beauty ideal off into another thread?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T12:33:54-07:00","id":1225663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225646#post1225646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the end of the day, some material is designed to appeal to certain demographics over others. Content producers do this because they want to make money, and believe that demographic A will get offer more money for the content than demographic B will. As such they may include certain images or ideas that appeal to Demographic A but which Demographic B does not care for. That isn't necessarily a bad thing, in and of itself. In fact, I think it would be problematic to demand that content producers set out from the get-go to produce content that is inoffensive to Demographics A, B, C, D and everyone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'm reminded of a video that I recently watched which mentioned the idea that tribalism in video gaming fandom is not only an arbitrary social construct, but one cultivated by deliberate marketing for the sake of creating a dedicated consumer base.<br /> <br /> \u200bEven in cases of the statement &quot;artists that want to make money will produce content for an audience&quot; was a completely true and accurate response to the question of art that is sexualized, or otherwise plays into stereotypes, it would still raise the question of why that audience exists in the first place. The answer is probably not &quot;it's just a thing that happened as a result of random, incomprehensible, or otherwise completely natural factors and there's no getting around it&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy initial reference to The Birth of a Nation was probably a bit heavy handed, but I think still makes the point that art doesn't exactly exist in a politically neutral context, and that the capacity of something to be financially successful (as Birth was, to a rather staggering degree) can raise questions of its own, and occasionally disturbing ones.<br /> <br /> So I'm still going to point to that film in particular as a counter-argument to the sentiment of &quot;if you don't like it, just ignore it&quot; (which is alternately highly difficult and irresponsible with it being something that romanticises bigoted terrorists) and &quot;it's neutral and acceptable for artists to produce content for a known paying market&quot; (which would be an issue when the market that is willing to pay quite a bit for it consists of widespread bigots).<br /> <br /> \u200bReally, whenever something like this comes up around art that disproportionately sexualises women, I think it would be worth considering how the arguments would apply if made about eighty years ago with regards to illustrated and animated representations of African-American people.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T12:49:38-07:00","id":1225669,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> <br /> <br /> I concur. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225647#post1225647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because they're free to do whatever they want, while the women are just portrayed as sexual objects.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you put a sexually charged caricature of a woman next to a sexually charged caricature of man, they are both being sexually objectified, in my view anyways.<br /> <br /> I'm not a scholar of these issues, obviously.<br /> <br /> I think this goes back to who is doing the objectification and who is the target. Like Anubis puts, this is marketing.<br /> <br /> Sex sells.<br /> <br /> Its a sexual objectification slugfest as far as I can tell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225647#post1225647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hah, you're being glib. That's great, you know this is fictional representation, but it's still fiction that informs a lot of attitudes people have.<br /> <br /> My allies?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad that glibness and sidestepping are widespread and bi-partisan.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225647#post1225647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an oversimplification, and the 'go get me an apple while you're at it' is dismissive. By demanding a sharing of a focus, when one problem is not as bad as another, the more pressing problem is not getting the attention it deserves. This is especially important when it comes to government or societal reform, where attention is a primary currency.<br /> <br /> No one's villifying you. This is the 'whataboutism.' Saying women shouldn't be portrayed as sex objects isn't the same as saying you're a bad person.<br /> <br /> That said, your argument's a bit scattershot. Artists who choose to objectify people sexually, or choose not to, aren't forced into either stance by the government, but depending on the artist some might be reliant on their customer base.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, seems pretty simple and fitting to me. IS not dismissive if I'm reducing my needs to an apple too, would it be better if I said your needs were a watermelon?<br /> <br /> Who is demanding a shared focus? A certain type of feminist insisting they espouse equality? Or me for taking them up on it? I already spoke on this. Any individual activist has the right to do whatever they want with their time and energy, but the a true feminist movement belongs to all. There are prominent female feminist intelectuals, authors and activits working on male issues right now. They are out of fashion lately with certain communities, I wonder why?<br /> <br /> Who are you to say the problem is not bad enough? A guy who claims to not know about the damages on body image, and the importance of body image for mental health, caused by the monolothic portrayal of unreal bodies in media? Think you're overstepping a little yet? Not yet? Not even a little? Or doesn't it matter because it is for people that identify as male? Please, let us know.<br /> <br /> Talk about scattershot,.. When did the government come into this?<br /> <br /> Ha! People are not trying to vilify me? Dunno if you noticed, but this is a very left leaning area of the webz.<br /> <br /> Trying to educate me with cartoons about leftist issues jargon and now another cartoon comparing what I'm saying with &quot;all lives matter&quot;, trying to draw a connection between my feeling vilified because people are saying women shouldn't be portrayed as sexual objects, as if I held that belief.<br /> <br /> Please friend, I'm 35, I know when a picture of me is trying to be painted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T12:55:18-07:00","id":1225670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225656#post1225656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that both houses aren't on fire, the one house (sexually objectifying women) is on fire (the picture was posted), and all houses have a chance of being on fire (both men and women have negative portrayals in media), some more than others (women more so than men), and to different degrees (objectifying of women has been historically worse than that of men and is portrayed as passive and always sexual versus active and aspirational, even if unrealistically so). So when one person says my house is on fire, and that happens quite often and is prone to happen, saying my house also sometimes catches fire is 'whataboutism'.<br /> <br /> Nobody is saying that you can't advocate for better representation of male bodies in media, just do it when its the topic at hand rather than jumping in when someone is talking about a different thing in need of advocacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so it is alright for you to insert your topics wherever you want, but I have some approved times and ways to insert my topic.<br /> <br /> Your dismissal of my issues is my dismissal of yours. Isn't that nice?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T12:58:56-07:00","id":1225675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225670#post1225670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, so it is alright for you to insert your topics wherever you want, but I have some approved times and ways to insert my topic.<br /> <br /> Your dismissal of my issues is my dismissal of yours. Isn't that nice?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except its not, the start of this was a post of an image sexually objectifying women, if it had been an overly muscular and oiled up male, and you had said something about it being unrealistic and harmful and somebody else and gone 'but women get sexually objectified' then that would have been wrong too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T13:06:03-07:00","id":1225679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225663#post1225663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bMy initial reference to The Birth of a Nation was probably a bit heavy handed, but I think still makes the point that art doesn't exactly exist in a politically neutral context, and that the capacity of something to be financially successful (as Birth was, to a rather staggering degree) can raise questions of its own, and occasionally disturbing ones</div> </div> </div> </div>The intent behind the material matters. There is a <i>huge</i> difference between Birth of a Nation, which was specifically created for the specific purpose of mobilizing white people against black people and creating an atmosphere in which people would support the lynching of African-Americans and someone drawing some artwork that might be considered mysoginistic by some people.<br /> <br /> If we're looking at artwork which was created with the specific intent of demeaning women and encourages people to say, go out and attack them, then that would be in the same category as Birth of a Nation. But I haven't seen anyone posting that kind of artwork, and to suggest that artwork which happens to focus on a woman's butt or breasts or shows them in an erotic position is somehow comparable to a movie that was created to encourage white people to kill black people seems a bit off base.<br /> <br /> If you're flipping through the channels and see an episode of He-man and you don't like the way He-man or She-ra or whoever is presented in the show, what's the issue with just changing the channel? Comparing something like He-man to Birth of a Nation is, I feel, rather problematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-07-2018, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T13:08:09-07:00","id":1225680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225659#post1225659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. Just wow <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> No, the guy in the comic is not the bad guy. That comic is just about <i>impossible</i> to misread. He is just engaging in whataboutism, Just like you. You <i>are </i>that guy. He is also depicted in a manner you want men to be depicted. Average. He is not an Adonis, no, but he's not a hideous abomination either! He's just... average. And here you are, drawing away attention from that comic's message from how women are objectified to something which clearly is not there, yet another example of whataboutism. Yes, someone is indeed arguing in bad faith!<br /> <br /> You also ignore the by now many arguments about how sexually objectifying of women is not the same as the power fantasies of men. Batman is depicted that way by men for men, and if you wish to argue that is done in a way to make the readers want to have sex him him, allow me to laugh in your face. <i>It is not the same! </i>Unattainable aspirations that distort what a healthy body image should be is something else entirely. You wish to talk about that, dedicate another thread to it and do not entangle it with what is clearly a women's issue.<br /> <br /> This is not me dismissing that issue, nor me being blind to them. This is me <i>separating</i> them. After all, it's not as if women do not struggle with unattainable beauty ideals. But that's not the problem of being reduced to sex objects.<br /> <br /> And in regard to how feminism should also advocate men's rights, or it's not about equality. Also laughable. That is not how emancipation works. I suppose BLM should be advocating for white people too and those who fight poverty for the rights of the 1%'s. Yeah right.<br /> <br /> So could we please spin the beauty ideal off into another thread?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're right it is impossible to misread. Watching you try to say no malice was done attributing unattractive traits to the obvious bad guy of the story (series?) is entertaining. But not convincing. You can insist, but save yourself the trouble, is not gonna work on me. Somewhere along the way I convinced myself I'm fairly smart, and I'm stubborn to boot. And when I see a spade there is no way for you to talking me into thinking that I'm seeing something else.<br /> <br /> I started the thread to talk about free speech and art consuming rights. The thread drifts anyways it drifts... I'm not the thread topic police and neither are you.<br /> <br /> How about you take your own advice;<br /> <br /> &quot;If you want to talk about sexual objectification of women, don't entangle it with free speech, an issue for all humans. So can you please spin the sexual objectification idea off into another thread?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T13:10:12-07:00","id":1225681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225675#post1225675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except its not, the start of this was a post of an image sexually objectifying women, if it had been an overly muscular and oiled up male, and you had said something about it being unrealistic and harmful and somebody else and gone 'but women get sexually objectified' then that would have been wrong too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean, technically, the start of this was a debate about whether it is the right and correct thing to complain about these representations every time such an image is posted. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225320#post1225320\">My argument</a> on the matter has already been heard; I'm kind of waiting for a more substantial rebuttal than &quot;I disagree, because everybody here agrees with this complaint, so there is no need to repeat it&quot;. (I mean, if everyone <i>did</i> agree, then we... wouldn't really have to repeat the complaint, would we?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T13:13:24-07:00","id":1225683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225675#post1225675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Except its not, the start of this was a post of an image sexually objectifying women, if it had been an overly muscular and oiled up male, and you had said something about it being unrealistic and harmful and somebody else and gone 'but women get sexually objectified' then that would have been wrong too.</div> </div> </div> </div>By post I will assume you mean &quot;thread&quot;. And I'm glad to inform you that, no.<br /> <br /> This thread was started on free speech and art consuming. <br /> <br /> Other people, not me, shifted the topic. You do it so naturally that you don't even notice that you are part of the hijacking. I'm just along for the ride. <br /> <br /> Sorry if you don't like the noise I'm making on my plane that you are helping hijack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T13:15:34-07:00","id":1225684,"title":"","content":"TGUEIROS, this thread started as a result of my comments responding to you addressing somebody expressing a dislike of overly sexualised images of women with &quot;if you don't like something, just don't consume it&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bHow can you hold that belief in addition to the one that there's something wrong with pervasive ways in which men are artistically represented?<br /> <br /> \u200bYou can't have it both ways. You can't dismiss something as an issue because people are capable of ignoring it, at the same time as saying that it is an issue, but one that affects yourself as well.<br /> <br /> Which, given your response to Anubis, you still appear to be trying to do.<br /> <br /> \u200bI actually do start to find it a bit suspect when you first bring up the point somewhere along the line of my arguing against the attitude that problem representation of women can be simply ignored. I don't think you're lying, but I think it says something to your intent when it's brought up in that manner.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, given the trajectory of the conversation, it feels less like an argument for the sake of inclusion and more about trying to undermine people arguing against artistic representations of women by painting them as hypocrites.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat, I think, is the part that makes it feel like Whatabout-ism, because that's the manner in which I often see these things being brought up in feminist discussions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T13:18:06-07:00","id":1225685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225681#post1225681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I mean, technically, the start of this was a debate about whether it is the right and correct thing to complain about these representations every time such an image is posted. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225320#post1225320\">My argument</a> on the matter has already been heard; I'm kind of waiting for a more substantial rebuttal than &quot;I disagree, because everybody here agrees with this complaint, so there is no need to repeat it&quot;. (I mean, if everyone <i>did</i> agree, then we... wouldn't really have to repeat the complaint, would we?)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh sure, that's the purpose of the thread indeed. And I agree with your stance on the matter as well. As long as we sit idly by and let things that are harmful to people go then they will continue to be harmful.<br /> <br /> I was referring to the specific train of conversation that implied that it was equivelent to complain about objectification of men and women in art in response to a piece of art that is clearly only a problem for one of the two.<br /> <br /> Which just made me think of a thing worth pointing out on that train.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2746_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2746\" data-vbnamecard=\"2746\">TGUEIROS</a> , if no one had complained about the picture in the first place, would you have brought up objectification of men in art? If not then it is 'whataboutism' because it only came up because the other did.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Some comments that came in while I was typing.<br /> <br /> No I don't mean this thread, I mean the post on the Exalted Image thread that actually started this conversation. Naming this thread free speech doesn't remove it from the context that started it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":". 06-07-2018, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T13:23:31-07:00","id":1225688,"title":"","content":"Hmm, yes, I guess we're dealing with a MRA red piller troll. Oh well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T13:26:03-07:00","id":1225692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225681#post1225681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I mean, technically, the start of this was a debate about whether it is the right and correct thing to complain about these representations every time such an image is posted. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225320#post1225320\">My argument</a> on the matter has already been heard; I'm kind of waiting for a more substantial rebuttal than &quot;I disagree, because everybody here agrees with this complaint, so there is no need to repeat it&quot;. (I mean, if everyone <i>did</i> agree, then we... wouldn't really have to repeat the complaint, would we?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I disagree. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The inspirational art thread has traditionally been a place to post inspirational art without criticism.<br /> <br /> It is not supposed to be inspirational to everyone, or even the viewers, but to the one posting the images.<br /> <br /> It is sort of a safe space to post art that inspires YOUR Exalted, and if other people are inspired by it too, thats great!<br /> <br /> It is not the place to have your taste in art critiqued or to be educated on gender issues. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T13:27:54-07:00","id":1225694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225679#post1225679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If we're looking at artwork which was created with the specific intent of demeaning women and encourages people to say, go out and attack them, then that would be in the same category as Birth of a Nation. But I haven't seen anyone posting that kind of artwork, and to suggest that artwork which happens to focus on a woman's butt or breasts or shows them in an erotic position is somehow comparable to a movie that was created to encourage white people to kill black people seems a bit off base.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, the attitudes of people who go on killing sprees and say that it's because they're angry at being incels, or who make extended posts about there being no girls on the Internet because &quot;women in real life enjoy the advantage of people only ever listening to them and pretending that they're interesting because they want sex, which they lack on the Internet because of anonymity (and any time they break that anonymity they're just looking for attention)&quot;, those attitudes come from somewhere.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's implausible that part of the place where it comes from is a constant background noise of visual and narrative cues contributing to the basic formation of a world view in which women exist primarily for the sexual gratification of men.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere are definitely men who regard the idea that women are not sexually available to them as some kind of terrible betrayal, and are motivated by the resulting anger to acts of harassment or outright violence. I don't think the contribution to that of a ubiquity of portrayals that prioritise visual cues for sexual availability can be simply dismissed.<br /> <br /> \u200bSuddenly, I'm reminded of information concerning harassment at conventions, and the degree to which women cosplaying as characters whom they like whose default costuming is sexually provocative (with it being hard to find a character to like without such dress), has been taken as an invitation to unwanted touching. So there's another instance in which it leads to substantial harm.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T13:37:49-07:00","id":1225698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225684#post1225684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TGUEIROS, this thread started as a result of my comments responding to you addressing somebody expressing a dislike of overly sexualised images of women with &quot;if you don't like something, just don't consume it&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bHow can you hold that belief in addition to the one that there's something wrong with pervasive ways in which men are artistically represented?<br /> <br /> \u200bYou can't have it both ways. You can't dismiss something as an issue because people are capable of ignoring it, at the same time as saying that it is an issue, but one that affects yourself as well.<br /> <br /> Which, given your response to Anubis, you still appear to be trying to do.<br /> <br /> \u200bI actually do start to find it a bit suspect when you first bring up the point somewhere along the line of my arguing against the attitude that problem representation of women can be simply ignored. I don't think you're lying, but I think it says something to your intent when it's brought up in that manner.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, given the trajectory of the conversation, it feels less like an argument for the sake of inclusion and more about trying to undermine people arguing against artistic representations of women by painting them as hypocrites.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat, I think, is the part that makes it feel like Whatabout-ism, because that's the manner in which I often see these things being brought up in feminist discussions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isator, this post was started by me because of your response to what I said, yes.<br /> <br /> And that first response was to immediately tag me with an extremely charged Birth of the Nation thing, that I felt the need to clarify that yes I think people should be allowed to make Birth of the Nation, and also clarify that I abhor the ideologies of that film.<br /> <br /> That is what I wanted to discuss. Freedom to produce content and freedom not to consume it. That and the safe space status of the Inspirational Art thread.<br /> <br /> All this other stuff is thread drift, and I drifted into it with my life experiences and my views.<br /> <br /> Now people want to take ownership of the thread and tell me to leave, because they don't agree with me on a thread drift topic. The direct insults already started. Its just reality.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T13:39:29-07:00","id":1225700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225688#post1225688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, yes, I guess we're dealing with a MRA red piller troll. Oh well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep things civil please. <br /> <br /> If you don't want to talk to me just don't. <br /> <br /> No need to call me names.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T13:43:52-07:00","id":1225701,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1329_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1329\" data-vbnamecard=\"1329\">ElvesofZion</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225685#post1225685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2746_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2746\" data-vbnamecard=\"2746\">TGUEIROS</a> , if no one had complained about the picture in the first place, would you have brought up objectification of men in art? If not then it is 'whataboutism' because it only came up because the other did.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Some comments that came in while I was typing.<br /> <br /> No I don't mean this thread, I mean the post on the Exalted Image thread that actually started this conversation. Naming this thread free speech doesn't remove it from the context that started it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The post that started this conversation is the first post on this thread, which I made to discuss content production and consumption, the safe space status of the inspirational art thread and to answer a charged comment directed at me.<br /> <br /> You are free to start a post about whatever other post and subject you want to.<br /> <br /> Please be more self-aware and less self-righteous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 06-07-2018, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T13:49:07-07:00","id":1225704,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> <br /> <br /> About my beliefs...<br /> <br /> Do you really need an explanation about how a belief in free speech and agency can coexist with a perception that some things stink?<br /> <br /> Please don't think I want any laws made to fix this issue. But if there is a platform to try to change paradigms by free dicourse, it would be lovely if this could change too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T13:49:42-07:00","id":1225705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225694#post1225694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bWell, the attitudes of people who go on killing sprees and say that it's because they're angry at being incels, or who make extended posts about there being no girls on the Internet because &quot;women in real life enjoy the advantage of people only ever listening to them and pretending that they're interesting because they want sex, which they lack on the Internet because of anonymity (and any time they break that anonymity they're just looking for attention)&quot;, those attitudes come from somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>That may be an issue more with America than with media in general. There are plenty of countries in the world where women are sexualized just as much as in America (for example it's not uncommon on European TV to see topless women with the sole reason they're topless being to draw viewers) and that's on top of the American media they receive. At the same time, it doesn't seem like Europe has this same problem with &quot;incels&quot; that America does. So I don't know that we can necessarily point towards the sexualization of women in the media as the direct cause of &quot;incel's&quot;. Maybe there's a correlation there (and I'm not entirely certain that there is) but that also doesn't imply causation.<br /> <br /> Whether it's video games, movies, tabletop RPGs or even pornography, I always get a bit weary when people point towards media as the reason for why individuals choose to engage in violence or bad behavior and then use that as an argument for why we need to change or modify (or outright ban) that media.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-07-2018, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T13:54:50-07:00","id":1225708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225701#post1225701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1329_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1329\" data-vbnamecard=\"1329\">ElvesofZion</a><br /> <br /> The post that started this conversation is the first post on this thread, which I made to discuss content production and consumption, the safe space status of the inspirational art thread and to answer a charged comment directed at me.<br /> <br /> You are free to start a post about whatever other post and subject you want to.<br /> <br /> Please be more self-aware and less self-righteous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have read the whole thread (and the other one) and the posts that started in in the Exalted thread. I will also point out that you were the one who brought up the topic of male representation not being mentioned in the previous thread when female was (I just went back through this thread and checked). The post you were replying to was on topic for this thread in that it was stating that 'yes, despite the critical neutral state of the image thread, it was useful to continuingly bring up the bad female representation. You countered by bringing up male representation. <br /> <br /> The topic of art, criticism and freedom is well served by discussing the nuance of what is appropriate to say in response to what. Pretending that this thread exists in a vacuum is nonsense and is clearly only for you to impose on others not yourself.<br /> <br /> I'll be done with this since it is clearly not going anywhere. To summarize:<br /> <br /> Should art be criticized or simply ignored when it is harmful to people? It should be criticized and shamed even in a place where \u2018criticism is frowned upon\u2019. Harmfulness outweighs considerations of nicety.<br /> Is it respectful to bring up unrelated issues when someone is discussing how a piece of art continues a trend of harm towards a specific group? No, it\u2019s not respectful and false equivalency are harmful and whataboutism is harmful (even if \u2018unintentional\u2019).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T14:01:21-07:00","id":1225709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225708#post1225708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have read the whole thread (and the other one) and the posts that started in in the Exalted thread. I will also point out that you were the one who brought up the topic of male representation not being mentioned in the previous thread when female was (I just went back through this thread and checked). The post you were replying to was on topic for this thread in that it was stating that 'yes, despite the critical neutral state of the image thread, it was useful to continuingly bring up the bad female representation. You countered by bringing up male representation.<br /> <br /> The topic of art, criticism and freedom is well served by discussing the nuance of what is appropriate to say in response to what. Pretending that this thread exists in a vacuum is nonsense and is clearly only for you to impose on others not yourself.<br /> <br /> I'll be done with this since it is clearly not going anywhere. To summarize:<br /> <br /> Should art be criticized or simply ignored when it is harmful to people? It should be criticized and shamed even in a place where \u2018criticism is frowned upon\u2019. Harmfulness outweighs considerations of nicety.<br /> Is it respectful to bring up unrelated issues when someone is discussing how a piece of art continues a trend of harm towards a specific group? No, it\u2019s not respectful and false equivalency are harmful and whataboutism is harmful (even if \u2018unintentional\u2019).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for confirming what I said about your views.<br /> <br /> You think you can insert your concerns wherever you please, but other people should follow rules.<br /> <br /> I never said the topic was sacrosanct. I was just logically answering yours and others baseless calls for me to create another thread to discuss thread drift. When you, yourselves, are thread drifting.<br /> <br /> Logic and consistency. Try it sometime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T14:03:56-07:00","id":1225710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225692#post1225692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I disagree. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The inspirational art thread has traditionally been a place to post inspirational art without criticism.<br /> <br /> It is not supposed to be inspirational to everyone, or even the viewers, but to the one posting the images.<br /> <br /> It is sort of a safe space to post art that inspires YOUR Exalted, and if other people are inspired by it too, thats great!<br /> <br /> It is not the place to have your taste in art critiqued or to be educated on gender issues.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You do seem to be correct - as much as I disagree with the mission statement of a community resource thread not being focused on providing useful content to the community, the thread is what it is.<br /> <br /> I guess the only recourse we have to combat not-useful content is to post useful content of our own in response in a slightly passive-aggressive way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T14:05:19-07:00","id":1225711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225700#post1225700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Keep things civil please.<br /> <br /> If you don't want to talk to me just don't.<br /> <br /> No need to call me names.</div> </div> </div> </div>While there's a fair point, there's also a case of calling a spade a spade.<br /> <br /> I get if you don't identify as those things and even take offense to it, but when your points of view and method of argumentation fit the bill, shouldn't that also be a cause for consideration that maybe you're presenting yourself in a way you don't want to be seen?<br /> <br /> Cause I gotta say, the spade looks an awful lot like a spade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keii