sometime.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have no idea what you mean here. I never accused you of thread drift, nor suggested that you should start a new thread. I said that rather than accusing others of thread drift, you should own the fact that that current train of conversation was started by you, not by other people.<br /> <br /> If you didnt want to discuss the side topic, then don't. Say it is against the thread, and move on. You argued about it for many posts before starting to use the thread drift comment as a way to stop the people who disagreed with you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225712#post1225712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess the question is, was <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://cdna.artstation.com/p/assets/images/images/010/811/274/large/wl-op-44s.jpg?1526359591\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div> disrespectful and harmful and does it deserve to be compared to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Birth_of_a_Nation\" target=\"_blank\">Birth of a Nation</a>?<br /> <br /> I don't really believe so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that a direct comparison to Birth of a Nation was hyperbolic (as did the person who originally said it). It is likley closer to something like how black people still tend to play subservient roles or die off first in American movies and television. One more in a string of problematic elements within an industry plagued with problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T14:21:48-07:00","id":1225721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225714#post1225714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you aluminiumtrioxid!<br /> <br /> For a reasonable, lighthearted and funny post!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You laugh, but I have <i>hundreds of images </i>saved on my hard drive :P<br /> <br /> I can post women of color, older women, reasonably dressed women, or women who look physically strong and combat-ready for every single picture of a half-naked chick with a sword in her hand, and keep this up for a <i>very long time</i>.<br /> <br /> And the community shall see that useful content is being shared, and there shall be much rejoicing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T14:22:22-07:00","id":1225722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225705#post1225705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That may be an issue more with America than with media in general. There are plenty of countries in the world where women are sexualized just as much as in America (for example it's not uncommon on European TV to see topless women with the sole reason they're topless being to draw viewers) and that's on top of the American media they receive. At the same time, it doesn't seem like Europe has this same problem with &quot;incels&quot; that America does. So I don't know that we can necessarily point towards the sexualization of women in the media as the direct cause of &quot;incel's&quot;. Maybe there's a correlation there (and I'm not entirely certain that there is) but that also doesn't imply causation.<br /> <br /> Whether it's video games, movies, tabletop RPGs or even pornography, I always get a bit weary when people point towards media as the reason for why individuals choose to engage in violence or bad behavior and then use that as an argument for why we need to change or modify (or outright ban) that media.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, as a European, our countries are not better than the US. I'd like to see us elect a poc as a president in one of our presidents/pm's. #metoo also did not originate here. You might have a clown as a president right now and he <i>is</i> doing damage, but don't count yourselves out, and don't buy into us euro's being in any way morally superior beings.<br /> <br /> We definitely have all that bad behavior too, the violence less so. As we have the media too, that can't be the cause for it. Better social security and healthcare combined with less access to firearms is what makes the difference in my opinion. Give our teenagers guns and no prospects for a life worth living and they'd be shooting up schools too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T14:22:48-07:00","id":1225723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225715#post1225715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh ArcaneArts. I accept that people may label me MRA or Red Piller or whatever else. Whatever helps them fit me into their neat little boxes. Don't care.<br /> <br /> But not a troll. If I'm not mistaken, calling people trolls is insulting, and insulting is against forum policy.<br /> <br /> I am saddened that you advocate breaking forum rules when you disagree with people.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll note I said there's a fair point, because yes, it is against forum rules, and yes, there's better ways to express that opinion. It just wasn't my central point.<br /> <br /> That being &quot;If it bothers you enough to call it out, maybe you should consider it was done for a reason.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you don't like being called a troll, then maybe you should reconsider how you handle conversations. You don't come across like you're actually considering other people's points and engaging in thoughtful consideration, you read like someone evoking a more sophisticated &quot;u mad bro.&quot;<br /> <br /> But hey, you don't care, so that pretty much spells it out explicitly. Have at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T14:33:24-07:00","id":1225726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225717#post1225717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have no idea what you mean here. I never accused you of thread drift, nor suggested that you should start a new thread. I said that rather than accusing others of thread drift, you should own the fact that that current train of conversation was started by you, not by other people.<br /> <br /> If you didnt want to discuss the side topic, then don't. Say it is against the thread, and move on. You argued about it for many posts before starting to use the thread drift comment as a way to stop the people who disagreed with you.<br /> <br /> ..</div> </div> </div> </div>Read all posts. All the thread drift discussion started a certain person asking me to leave to discuss thread drift, when we're all thread drifting.<br /> <br /> I just clarified this is not the &quot;sexual objectification of women in art&quot; thread. Which it seems is what they thought it was.<br /> <br /> I have a strong impression you piled on to that. And if that is wrong, I apologize, it is not a matter worth discussing much.<br /> <br /> But the rules respecting thing, and how you believe you're exempt from it, stands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date"