ism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225726#post1225726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Read all posts. All the thread drift discussion started a certain person asking me to leave to discuss thread drift, when we're all thread drifting.<br /> <br /> I just clarified this is not the &quot;sexual objectification of women in art&quot; thread. Which it seems is what they thought it was.<br /> <br /> I have a strong impression you piled on to that. And if that is wrong, I apologize, it is not a matter worth discussing much.<br /> <br /> But the rules respecting thing, and how you believe you're exempt from it, stands.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly was not saying anything about starting a new thread at any point. I was only responding to posts as I had a response that were on topic (to that sub conversation at least, which I do consider to be on topic since it was part of the justification about when and where it is appropriate to criticized art and how).<br /> <br /> I am still unsure of what situation you believe the rules respecting thing you mean. The only 'rule' I have advocated for is that it is in actively harmful to partake in whataboutism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T14:49:52-07:00","id":1225735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225723#post1225723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll note I said there's a fair point, because yes, it is against forum rules, and yes, there's better ways to express that opinion. It just wasn't my central point.<br /> <br /> That being &quot;If it bothers you enough to call it out, maybe you should consider it was done for a reason.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you don't like being called a troll, then maybe you should reconsider how you handle conversations. You don't come across like you're actually considering other people's points and engaging in thoughtful consideration, you read like someone evoking a more sophisticated &quot;u mad bro.&quot;<br /> <br /> But hey, you don't care, so that pretty much spells it out explicitly. Have at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a bit intrigued. Why did you single out the one thing I took issue with to say I don't care about it? Seems strange... Did you misunderstand?<br /> <br /> Are you in the habit of questioning the way you act after being insulted?<br /> <br /> Should a woman reconsider the way she presents herself after being called a slut on the streets?<br /> <br /> Do you think the first response of the targets of incivility should be to question what is their fault on the matter?<br /> <br /> I don't know if you realize this, but this is eerily close to espousing victim-blaming and self-loathing. Things I sincerely believe you are not for.<br /> <br /> I thought a troll is some one who acts in a way to specifically rile people up. Am I mistaken? Because if not, then I am definetely not a troll, do take issue with being called one, and don't think I need to re examine anything about that.<br /> <br /> So yes I do care. That is why I asked to not be called it.<br /> <br /> So please extend me some humanity instead of dismissing me as grouping of ideas you don't like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 06-07-2018, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T14:54:23-07:00","id":1225736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225733#post1225733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I certainly was not saying anything about starting a new thread at any point. I was only responding to posts as I had a response that were on topic (to that sub conversation at least, which I do consider to be on topic since it was part of the justification about when and where it is appropriate to criticized art and how).<br /> <br /> I am still unsure of what situation you believe the rules respecting thing you mean. The only 'rule' I have advocated for is that it is in actively harmful to partake in whataboutism.</div> </div> </div> </div>How you feel that despite the rules (no criticism in inspirational thread) are alright to break. But I can't break your rules (speak about men's issues when talking about women's issues).<br /> <br /> It is a very common symptom of self-righteousness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 06-07-2018, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T15:01:52-07:00","id":1225738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225736#post1225736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How you feel that despite the rules (no criticism in inspirational thread) are alright to break. But I can't break your rules (speak about men's issues when talking about woman's issues).<br /> <br /> It is a very common sympton of self-righteousness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is a difference in rules there. Not all 'rules' are made equal. <br /> <br /> In this specific case, I believe the intent of the no criticizing rule of that thread is to keep the conversation civil, and to keep it flowing. The idea is to keep the flow of images coming and not stifle creativity. That's great. But if an image is posted that is considered harmful, then it is acceptable to break that civility rule to point it out because preventing harm is more important than general civility (this is what self defense and protest is all about, breaking rules where it is appropriate).<br /> <br /> If you can't see that some rules are worth breaking (Rosa Parks on a bus anyone?) while others are not, then there is no way you and I will ever be able to agree on anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T15:04:53-07:00","id":1225739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Angwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225722#post1225722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, as a European, our countries are not better than the US. I'd like to see us elect a poc as a president in one of our presidents/pm's. #metoo also did not originate here. You might have a clown as a president right now and he <i>is</i> doing damage, but don't count yourselves out, and don't buy into us euro's being in any way morally superior beings.<br /> <br /> We definitely have all that bad behavior too, the violence less so. As we have the media too, that can't be the cause for it. Better social security and healthcare combined with less access to firearms is what makes the difference in my opinion. Give our teenagers guns and no prospects for a life worth living and they'd be shooting up schools too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, I haven't heard of too many accounts of &quot;incels&quot; going on rampages and murdering people in Europe. You guys do have your share of violence though, as well as racism and whatnot. Still, I think when we're looking at the &quot;incel&quot; issue and why certain young men choose to engage in mass killings, we can just as easily point towards access to weaponry, or many, many other factors, some of which you mentioned.<br /> <br /> Unrealistic portrayals of men and women in the media are an issue (to a degree), but I don't think it's something that drives people to engage in mass killings like isator suggested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-07-2018, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T15:18:55-07:00","id":1225743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225738#post1225738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There is a difference in rules there. Not all 'rules' are made equal.<br /> <br /> In this specific case, I believe the intent of the no criticizing rule of that thread is to keep the conversation civil, and to keep it flowing. The idea is to keep the flow of images coming and not stifle creativity. That's great. But if an image is posted that is considered harmful, then it is acceptable to break that civility rule to point it out because preventing harm is more important than general civility (this is what self defense and protest is all about, breaking rules where it is appropriate).<br /> <br /> If you can't see that some rules are worth breaking (Rosa Parks on a bus anyone?) while others are not, then there is no way you and I will ever be able to agree on anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please refrain from escalating things so much. You just Birth of the Nation'ed this thread all over again. Rosa Parks! Seriously!? Are you truly talking about that kind of activism, protest and civil disobedience?! NO!<br /> <br /> Those rights are unequivocably established in the mind of any decent person. Any person who would question that doesn't merit my listening.<br /> <br /> On the matter of the actual discussion:<br /> <br /> Ok, excuse me while I feel free to discuss issues that partially caused 19 years of depression in my life (and severe consequences for many other guys I know) when I feel it is appropriate to do so. I'm not invading a Women's March podium taking a microphone and talking about men's issue here. I'm going stream of conscious style on very niche corner of the internet, talking about a very niche subject. It is not an extremely crucial emergency we're dealing with here.<br /> <br /> You are not the judge of when or which rules should be broken.<br /> <br /> I haven't heard a convincing argument yet as to why I shouldn't ask for boys issues to be considered when talking about comic/rpg art sensitivity raising efforts.<br /> <br /> You can call me MRA, Red PIll, or whatever else. You can allude to racism. You can try to associate me with everything that you consider ugly.<br /> <br /> You are still not doing a single productive thing to enact any positive change in me, not that you should try or care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 06-07-2018, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T15:20:37-07:00","id":1225744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225739#post1225739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unrealistic portrayals of men and women in the media are an issue (to a degree), but I don't think it's something that drives people to engage in mass killings like isator suggested.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a simplification of what I was saying, which was about the formation of world view.<br /> <br /> \u200bSure, when a death happens, it's facilitated by the availability of weapons and factors that inform a world view that is particular to violence. But when somebody expresses a motivation in terms of resentment of women, it raises the question of what the basis of that resentment is.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat was an extreme example mostly to validate any vague comparisons to the film, but an overall background noise that informs the formation of a world view in which women are absent and unwelcome from one's insular groups, or disrespected as a matter of course, is not bad solely in the examples of when it causes death. It's a terrible thing to live with as well. It's all part of a spectrum.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy objections don't start and stop with artistic representations in the fantasy genre, or any other; things are interconnected. This is just one that is more overt, and also matters a bit more here because it's related to the subject of forum discussion and the matter of how welcoming the hobby is.<br /> <br /> Don't forget what I was saying about cosplay and conventions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T15:22:05-07:00","id":1225745,"title":"","content":"Well, for what its worth, Brazil doesn't have incel mass shootings either. And the social safety net and life perspective is pretty shitty for a great majority of the population.<br /> <br /> And I don't think I need to speak on the country's record on sexualizing women.<br /> <br /> So by process of elimination... Gun control?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 06-07-2018, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T15:35:06-07:00","id":1225751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225744#post1225744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a simplification of what I was saying, which was about the formation of world view.<br /> <br /> \u200bSure, when a death happens, it's facilitated by the availability of weapons and factors that inform a world view that is particular to violence. But when somebody expresses a motivation in terms of resentment of women, it raises the question of what the basis of that resentment is.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat was an extreme example mostly to validate any vague comparisons to the film, but an overall background noise that informs the formation of a world view in which women are absent and unwelcome from one's insular groups, or disrespected as a matter of course, is not bad solely in the examples of when it causes death. It's a terrible thing to live with as well. It's all part of a spectrum.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy objections don't start and stop with artistic representations in the fantasy genre, or any other; things are interconnected. This is just one that is more overt, and also matters a bit more here because it's related to the subject of forum discussion and the matter of how welcoming the hobby is.<br /> <br /> Don't forget what I was saying about cosplay and conventions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think there has been a change in men's attitude and actions towards female nudity since the advent of this form of media?<br /> <br /> Do you think there would be a different outcome in these interactions if there was a such convention in the 1900s? Would there be more agression or less?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T16:15:36-07:00","id":1225758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225743#post1225743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please refrain from escalating things so much. You just Birth of the Nation'ed this thread all over again. Rosa Parks! Seriously!? Are you truly talking about that kind of activism, protest and civil disobedience?! NO!<br /> <br /> Those rights are unequivocably established in the mind of any decent person. Any person who would question that doesn't merit my listening.<br /> <br /> On the matter of the actual discussion:<br /> <br /> Ok, excuse me while I feel free to discuss issues that partially caused 19 years of depression in my life (and severe consequences for many other guys I know) when I feel it is appropriate to do so. I'm not invading a Women's March podium taking a microphone and talking about men's issue here. I'm going stream of conscious style on very niche corner of the internet, talking about a very niche subject. It is not an extremely crucial emergency we're dealing with here.<br /> <br /> You are not the judge of when or which rules should be broken.<br /> <br /> I haven't heard a convincing argument yet as to why I shouldn't ask for boys issues to be considered when talking about comic/rpg art sensitivity raising efforts.<br /> <br /> You can call me MRA, Red PIll, or whatever else. You can allude to racism. You can try to associate me with everything that you consider ugly.<br /> <br /> You are still not doing a single productive thing to enact any positive change in me, not that you should try or care.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly (and I mean this), Rosa Parks is just my go to example for protesting. Always has been.<br /> <br /> I was not implying that you were racist; though I can see where it may come off that way. And I was not the one who used the terms MRA or Red Pill or the one who said anything about them being used. You may want to try to separate the people in your life who have wronged you from those you think have wronged you.<br /> <br /> I will add that I am a White (Jewish) Cis Het Man from a small town who was scrawny and geeky as a child and spent most of my life being beat up and made fun of for not conforming to the idea of masculinity that was expected by the bigger boys around me. But I have learned to respect other peoples issues when they are brought up.<br /> <br /> I alone am not the judge no, but this thread was a discussion about when it was appropriate to criticize art and when not. I and others have laid out our opinions and provided arguments to back them up. The fact that you seem to be unwilling to engage with your own thread in good faith on that matter means I will again say I am done and will not be responding again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T16:33:43-07:00","id":1225762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225739#post1225739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit, I haven't heard of too many accounts of &quot;incels&quot; going on rampages and murdering people in Europe. You guys do have your share of violence though, as well as racism and whatnot. Still, I think when we're looking at the &quot;incel&quot; issue and why certain young men choose to engage in mass killings, we can just as easily point towards access to weaponry, or many, many other factors, some of which you mentioned.<br /> <br /> Unrealistic portrayals of men and women in the media are an issue (to a degree), but I don't think it's something that drives people to engage in mass killings like isator suggested.</div> </div> </div> </div>It pays to notice that &quot;incels&quot; have always been around, even explicitly, and no one paid any heed to them until a couple went into a murderous spree. The people that get labeled incels... they are pretty harmless, if tormented.<br /> <br /> Incel is just a &quot;new&quot; name to a kind of man that always existed: The ultimate loser. The person that for some reason just can't be sexually/romantically interesting to anyone, even if just by comparison: curiously enough, things like a wealthy community and sexual freedom aggravate this by raising people's standards. Nothing to do about that though, so solutions must come from somewhere else.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s12144-000-1017-5\" target=\"_blank\">This</a> <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/19726219\" target=\"_blank\">type</a> <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC2792572/\" target=\"_blank\">of</a> <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/12137144\" target=\"_blank\">person</a> <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/12021415\" target=\"_blank\">is</a> <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/12374437\" target=\"_blank\">kinda doomed</a> <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/16594799\" target=\"_blank\">to</a> <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/18476760\" target=\"_blank\">forever</a> <a href=\"https://kuscholarworks.ku.edu/handle/1808/1504\" target=\"_blank\">be</a> <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/11276907\" target=\"_blank\">like</a> that, and almost literally dies because of loneliness (this deprivation is associated with a <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/18394861\" target=\"_blank\">lot</a> <a href=\"https://econtent.hogrefe.com/doi/10.1027/1614-0001.28.3.103\" target=\"_blank\">of</a> <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/25910392\" target=\"_blank\">health</a> <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4021390/\" target=\"_blank\">issues</a> like <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/22042880\" target=\"_blank\">heart</a> diseases), and as such eventually things like support groups pop up.<br /> <br /> <br /> And on the incels going postal... Can you really point to the loser personality as the root cause of the rampancy? Their state, as far as we could tell, is not very different from that of most &quot;postal&quot; murderers: unstable psyche coupled with aggravating circumstances. The loser condition is just one of many that stress people out. The incel panic is just 2018's satanic panic, it will pass. Sadly, it will most likely pass without more resources being directed at the actual roots of these problems","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T16:59:48-07:00","id":1225773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225751#post1225751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think there has been a change in men's attitude and actions towards female nudity since the advent of this form of media?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think actual nudity is less titillating than clothing that emphasizes and mildly conceals a woman's secondary sexual characteristics.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut in talking about art intended to titillate... I do actually think that there's a difference in attitude to the kind of art that would have started around the covers of pulp fantasy anthologies in the 1930s or so (thin, busty, scantily clad, occasionally draped around the leg of a burly, manly hero), and something like a nude portrait of a woman from the Regency era (who might often be actually nude, have a realistic figure, and what I might interpret as a posture of confidence). I think there's a difference of context; one in which artists are exploring a breach in taboos about female nudity in an era of attempting growth of sexual freedom (which Victorian puritanical attitudes were a reaction to), and the other for the sake of marketing something with broad appeal in a reactionary post-suffrage world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUIEROS</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think there would be a different outcome in these interactions if there was a such convention in the 1900s? Would there be more agression or less?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the early 1900s? One is talking about an era in which women being so exposed would be scandalous, and possibly criminal.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhich amounts to a different method of controlling female sexuality and treating it as a public commodity, so there you go.<br /> <br /> \u200bI do think that con harassment is a bit of a throwback to a time in which pinching or slapping at the bottom of a women in the service industry, or to whom one was attracted, was an expected, even acceptable, behaviour.<br /> <br /> \u200bI would place that after a point at which public sexual contact was something taboo, and in a bit of an interim phase of periods in which women were asserting their civil rights (which would have included attitudes of presenting and controlling their own sexuality).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T18:47:43-07:00","id":1225788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225758#post1225758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Honestly (and I mean this), Rosa Parks is just my go to example for protesting. Always has been.<br /> <br /> I was not implying that you were racist; though I can see where it may come off that way. And I was not the one who used the terms MRA or Red Pill or the one who said anything about them being used. You may want to try to separate the people in your life who have wronged you from those you think have wronged you.<br /> <br /> I will add that I am a White (Jewish) Cis Het Man from a small town who was scrawny and geeky as a child and spent most of my life being beat up and made fun of for not conforming to the idea of masculinity that was expected by the bigger boys around me. But I have learned to respect other peoples issues when they are brought up.<br /> <br /> I alone am not the judge no, but this thread was a discussion about when it was appropriate to criticize art and when not. I and others have laid out our opinions and provided arguments to back them up. The fact that you seem to be unwilling to engage with your own thread in good faith on that matter means I will again say I am done and will not be responding again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elves, I apologize, for not keeping completely separate arguments for different people on these exchanges. Sorry for the spill over.<br /> <br /> I wasn't implying that it was you that called me those things when I used them to respond to you. I was making a general statement about people painting me a certain way, because of the Rosa Parks thing, that you acknowledged could be misconstrued.<br /> <br /> I don't get why you think I'm doing this in bad faith. I have poured a lot of energy into this. Magnitudes more than I should, not because I'm a troll with nothing better to do, but because I truly believe in what I'm saying here and value you all as people enough that I want to reach an understanding with as many as you as possible. Its just a personality trait of mine, I seek some common ground to stand with people on.<br /> <br /> I was truly happy when I found that with aluminiumtrioxid. I don't think we changed each others point of view on truly important things, but that we agreed on one of the core topics of the thread and parted ways amiably on the other issues was a great thing in my eyes.<br /> <br /> But I have my ideas and convictions, my experiences. And I wont betray those, I am truly open to be persuaded, its just that on these things the arguments haven't been enough. Maybe no argument will be enough for certain things. But I don't need to vilify you, label you, and put you in a box called &quot;people I don't like&quot; or &quot;not a person worthy of consideration&quot; you know? Those are reserved for truly severe offenses, which I believe none of us committed.<br /> <br /> So, however bad you find my opinion on this matter, I hope you can relate to what I'm saying on this post and that this could be our common ground to amiably part ways on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T18:59:34-07:00","id":1225792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225773#post1225773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> \u200bI do think that con harassment is a bit of a throwback to a time in which pinching or slapping at the bottom of a women in the service industry, or to whom one was attracted, was an expected, even acceptable, behaviour.<br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we are in agreement on everything, and the unsnipped part was what I was particularly thinking about when I posed the question.<br /> <br /> I dunno if it was me but I thought people were entering a set theory vibe trying figure shit out by inclusions and exclusions... I tend to fall into this mindset, but I know that everything can't be simply mathematical. For better and worse.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T14:25:18-07:00","id":1226296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225788#post1225788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get why you think I'm doing this in bad faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to go back over what happened here, as I see it. To be clear, though, I don't think you're <i>consciously</i> doing this. I feel that people mostly internalize views and opinions and lines of argument from the people around them, and that you've internalized one that was constructed in a particularly manipulative fashion by others in order to oppose and suppress views they disagreed with. I also think that a lot of this is driven by emotional reactions leading you to grasp for whatever argument you can that will put you in the right, so to speak.<br /> <br /> But anyway, let's go back. It started with this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/411718-inspirational-art-exalted-3e-edition?p=1225210#post1225210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hugely awesome art style. Not a big fan of the &quot;women hate clothes&quot; trope, however. A chance wasted. Then again, if you're that good an artist, you can draw whatever the fuck you want and don't have to deal with my complaints.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, this is an entirely uncontroversial statement of opinion. People form their views by listening to others around them and by adapting to a community; therefore, I believe we have not just a right but a duty to express views that we hold strongly. If you disagree, there's a lot of ways you can reply! But you responded to that with <i>this</i>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/411718-inspirational-art-exalted-3e-edition?p=1225251#post1225251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Art.<br /> <br /> Don't like it, don't consume it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What were you saying there? &quot;Nobody should ever express opinions on art that they disagree with?&quot; That's a nonsensical statement to take. Free speech requires free and open discourse; beyond that, any cultural values worth having are also worth repeating and reinforcing. What I think happened is that Cheshire Cat's statement pinged against the aspects of the script you've internalized that identify the <i>enemy</i>. Your reply probably felt natural and obvious to you (as part of a culture you've subsumed yourself in), but it was scripted to derail and essentially &quot;body-block&quot; Cheshire Cat's opinion - sending a message if &quot;ignore this person.&quot; It doesn't allow for any sort of answer or debate, and it contains a bunch of unstated assumptions about where Cheshire Cat is coming from and what they're trying to do intended to turn the audience against them.<br /> <br /> As we'll see, these become more explicit as the conversation goes on and we get deeper into your script. Your next post doubles starts to unload the script's full line of derailment and tactical positioning:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/411718-inspirational-art-exalted-3e-edition?p=1225270#post1225270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you argue against someone's right to imagine and create it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that <i>nobody</i>, at any point, had mentioned the right to do it up until then. You immediately moved to that point because doing so gave you a chance to grandstand about &quot;free speech&quot;, derailing the topic further and moving further away from the culture position you were trying to suppress. You weren't able to accurately assess what people were saying - you'd been trained to react to &quot;the enemy&quot; in a specific way using a specific set of ingrained talking points, stonewalling any sort of discussion. The goal is to shut them down whenever you encounter them without engaging what they're actually saying. You reiterate the talking point about &quot;don't like, don't buy, shut up&quot;, then paradoxically proceed with:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, please don't take this as me saying nobody can or should criticize art. Everyone can and should. Only there is an approrpiate place for it. This thread specifically asks to leave commentary out. </div> </div> </div>For the record, aside from some later statements by you, there's nothing in the thread that I could find asking for commentary to be left out; certainly there's nothing in the first post or first few pages about that. Commentary is often the best part of thinking about art.<br /> <br /> Also note your argument about an &quot;appropriate place&quot; even though your initial statement was pretty bluntly the opposite. Here your efforts to manipulate the discussion are particularly obvious; you <i>started</i> the debate by trying to silence Cheshire Cat, and continued to present arguments for why they should silence themselves throughout. But you simultaneously (without <i>any</i> grounding in fact, based solely on your insistence on following the script trained into you without regards for what anyone else was saying) implied that you were facing some nebulous forces of censorship. This part is an attempt to cover your own ass on that and to say &quot;oh, yes, you can say what you want, just not <i>here</i>, no, not in <i>that</i> tone, only in the appropriate place and the appropriate time--&quot;<br /> <br /> But obviously that's not your actual feeling. Based on your other statements it is pretty clear that your problem was with the content of Cheshire Cat's comment and not its simple existence. For instance:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And last I checked nudity is still ok, and I hope it forever is (I would miss Jen's scantily clad fellows also, if it wasn't, for the record). </div> </div> </div>You can't resist leaping to the assumption that Cheshire Cat is some sort of general anti-nudity crusader, loudly expressing your opposition to this imagined position; implicitly pushing that accusation solidifies your derailment above.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then you started this thread, with the incendiary and entirely-inaccurate title of &quot;art, criticism, and freedom&quot;. In it, you doubled down on your script (even though it's <i>still</i> the case that nobody but you was talking about censorship, and it's still the case that you were the one trying to silence others):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware#post1225302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I will never argue for total censorship.<br /> <br /> Restrict age of attendance, exhibition venue and hours, include disclaimers? Totally for it.<br /> <br /> Censorship? Never. The cost is immeasurable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminder for those keeping score: You have at this point in the conversation gone through three separate posts arguing why Cheshire Cat needs to shut up (responding to an <i>extremely mildly-worded</i> statement that Cheshire Cat personally did not like that art.) And yet you have the gall to accuse <i>others</i> of being censorious and acting like you're taking a stand in defense of free speech! This is not an argument made in good faith. Again, I don't mean to get inside your head - I can accept that you <i>feel</i> like you are arguing in good faith, that you internalized the script you're presenting here from others without fully stepping back to look at what it said overall - but the overall script you're following and the things you're saying? They are not a good-faith argument, at all. They're based around mustering the biggest emotional guns you can to silence an opinion you disagree with without having to confront it head-on.<br /> <br /> When you actually come to confront it in this thread, where do you go with it? &quot;Men face problems with sexualization, too, so we should focus on both?&quot; Well, that's an excellent point, but shouldn't you be <i>happy</i> that Cheshire Cat was willing to discuss how they felt about what they perceived as gratuitous sexualization? After all, it's not a zero-sum game. Yet it hit a button in your head to unfurl the script I outlined above.<br /> <br /> So here's what I'm seeing. You talk about wanting to find common ground; but when Cheshire Cat brought up their personal feelings, you jumped down their throat. My feeling is that you've been fed (and have internalized) a script that was <i>intentionally</i> written to be abrasive and insulting to potential allies on the female side of the discussion. You didn't see anything wrong, I suspect, with the way you confronted Cheshire Cat; then, when people treat your own commitment to men's issues or equality as disingenuous, you're confused. This is because the script you've unknowingly internalized is intended to isolate you from them and turn them against you.<br /> <br /> Nobody in this thread has actually criticized or doubted your experiences as a man; but <i>you</i> have (unbidden) criticized and repeatedly tried to silence someone who brought up their personal feelings about female sexualization. This says to me that you have a problem with that discussion and that part of you views this as a zero-sum game with your own experiences. You're not alone in this (lots of people feel that way about their own problems); but if you want to become an ally to the people who have problems with the sexualization of women, and work with them to address similar problems with men, then you need to be able to, at the very least, let that feeling go so you're capable of sitting and listening to their concerns without immediately telling them to shut up or changing the subject to your own. (You're free to argue with them if you want, but... nobody's gonna see you as an ally if you keep starting discussions by doing that.)<br /> <br /> Sometimes you'll find people getting up in your face telling <i>you</i> to shut up because women have it worse or whatever! This is normal. Those are people with the same issues you have. Recognize that you've been doing the same thing in the past, which should give you the understanding you need to avoid holding it against them. Being willing to sometimes brush off those people rather than fixating them as wounds in your head and carrying them as a grievance to armor you against ever seeking common cause with anyone in the future is unhealthy and unhelpful. You can, if you want, listen and consider and think about the problems women have, and connect them to the problems you've faced in your own life, and build a common coalition with anyone who's willing to listen to you, and <i>ignore</i> anyone who's just being an idiot or who plainly just has a chip on their shoulder and wants to fight you.<br /> <br /> But you can't do it if you come across as having a chip on your shoulder yourself, or if your first reaction to someone saying they feel sexualization of women is gratuitous is to tell them to shut up, your second reaction is to accuse them of censorship and start waving your FREEDOM flag, and your third reaction is to get all pensive and to say that men have it bad, too. That is - even if you don't recognize it - not a script intended to build bridges or to help you find a common cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 06-10-2018, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T14:59:18-07:00","id":1226303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1226296#post1226296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the record, aside from some later statements by you, there's nothing in the thread that I could find asking for commentary to be left out; certainly there's nothing in the first post or first few pages about that.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/411718-inspirational-art-exalted-3e-edition?p=478155#post478155\">Post #59</a> from the OP asks exactly that, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-10T16:02:19-07:00","id":1226315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1226303#post1226303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/411718-inspirational-art-exalted-3e-edition?p=478155#post478155\">Post #59</a> from the OP asks exactly that, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! That's page four, though, so not many people newly-arriving in the thread are likely to see it - and, in any case, responding to a one-line comment by confronting it (rather than just ignoring it) is doing the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T08:03:03-07:00","id":1226458,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar517_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"517\" data-vbnamecard=\"517\">Aquillion</a> <br /> <br /> This thread and the arguments contained in them are pretty long, spread and tiresome. I'll do my best to address some of your points, but I won't go through all the gender issues stuff again, my view on them seems pretty clear, and I don't think you want to discuss them per se, so I'll move on to clarify my view some things you've said.<br /> <br /> 1. Me &quot;jumping on Cheshire's throat&quot; and trying to silence them.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but I don't see any instance of that. I didn't even address them directly, didn't ask them not to criticize, didn't ask the to shut up, didn't ask them to take it somewhere else... So, where are you getting this from? I just stated my stance towards art production/consumption in a dry and direct way. But I didn't try to censor Cheshire in that thread. I just gave my tangential opinion on the matter.<br /> <br /> It was actually Synapse, who expressed exasperation about those types of comments, and my comment was made to express my view and mildly support his exasperation.<br /> <br /> The discussion about propriety when speaking, and arguments about where and when to do so, only came in this thread when people tried to censor me from speaking about whatever I wanted to speak because &quot;reasons and rules&quot; that they feel are only alright to break when it serves their purpose.<br /> <br /> People are devising and establishing all these arcane rules about how to talk and interact with each other, as if every conversation was a debate competition or a complex ritual with grave consequences for missteps. It is contrived and boring and doesn't serve any good purpose I can tell.<br /> <br /> Again, this thread is not about sexual objectification of women, it is about what I said on the topic and the first post. I treat these threads as regular conversation, topics drift, people change subjects, say things related and non related to the main topic. You know, natural flow, not some weird shit full of rules. The rules here are those of the overall forum, not what anyone wants to say they are.<br /> <br /> If you wanna talk about one specific thing in this forum, how about you make a thread about it? Then you can ask people to stay on topic if they deviate. Isn't that a simple rule to remember and follow? <br /> <br /> 2. Freedom.<br /> <br /> That post was made after Isator brought Birth of the Nation as an example of abominable art that was made. It was hyperbolic and while I can't know people's minds, it seemed it was done to either invalidate my view or tag me with something very ugly. And I made this thread to respond to that.<br /> <br /> My stance is pretty clear. People can produce whatever art they feel like producing. Let the marketplace of ideas sort it out. Work on your marketing to convince the people your views are better and the ones that should be consumed.<br /> <br /> 3. Chip on my shoulder.<br /> <br /> Well, if talking about my experiences and sticking to my views is having a chip on my shoulder, Aquillion, feel free to think believe that I have a few. It is just another label, which I also don't identify with or care about.<br /> <br /> 4. &quot;In good faith&quot;...<br /> <br /> Well, unless your thoughts are completely original, or you're extremely insulated, you were probably convinced of something by someone. So arguing as if this has any kind of absolute value as to whether a point of view is valid or not is not very effective. <br /> <br /> So do you have anything else to tell me about those views that other people on the thread haven't yet? If not, please accept my arguments in good faith, because I believe them, instead of taking me for a troll, or a naive simpleton, that is all I ask.<br /> <br /> Saying I can't say something because you said something is bullshit. in my view, and I don't care about it.<br /> <br /> You are free to disagree with that, and try to convince me otherwise, or not. I hope you don't think I'm bad because of that, but you're also free to do that too. <br /> <br /> Just remember the more nitpicky you are with people, the more you are creating a clique instead of a movement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T01:58:45-07:00","id":1226714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1226458#post1226458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Me &quot;jumping on Cheshire's throat&quot; and trying to silence them.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but I don't see any instance of that. I didn't even address them directly, didn't ask them not to criticize, didn't ask the to shut up</div> </div> </div> </div>From the first page of this thread:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1225367#post1225367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that context my response was very simple.<br /> <br /> In that thread, please, if you don't like something, and that something is not against the terms of use, please don't look at it, don't take it as inspiration for your Exalted, and shut up about it!</div> </div> </div> </div>That is how <i>you yourself</i> described your own comments. Your intent was to make them shut up. You didn't like what they were saying and wanted them to stop saying it; this emotional response drove you to search for an argument you could use to shut down that discussion. Everything else you've said has been driven by that same basic desire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The discussion about propriety when speaking, and arguments about where and when to do so, only came in this thread when people tried to censor me from speaking </div> </div> </div>You are the only one who has, at any point in this discussion, attempted to silence others. Fullstop. I'm not going to stop pointing this out every time you try to talk about censorship or FREEDOM\u2122. I assume (from the fact that you keep trying to work it in, despite its absurdity in this context) that this feeling that you're defending FREEDOM\u2122 is important to what drives your feelings on this topic, but in this case it's just... nonsensical, in the sense that it bears no relation to anything anyone but you has said so far.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People are devising and establishing all these arcane rules about how to talk and interact with each other, as if every conversation was a debate competition or a complex ritual with grave consequences for missteps. It is contrived and boring and doesn't serve any good purpose I can tell. </div> </div> </div>You are the one who specifically tried to silence someone by citing the rules of the thread! I'm just... I don't know what to say to this? This is <i>literally</i> how we started this, with you trying to create and invoke arcane rules restricting when Cheshire could or could not voice the opinion they voiced, with the explicit goal of making them (in your own words) <i>shut up</i>.<br /> <br /> I have <i>deconstructed</i> your arguments - going over why they seemed weird, out of place, and even nonsensical, then piecing together what I felt the underlying drive behind them was. And based on that I would <i>suggest</i> that you stop for a moment to consider both what you're saying and the underlying motivation driving it; but that's just a suggestion, based on the uncomfortably cringe-inducing way I see my past self in you.<br /> <br /> This sort of spiral can be escaped. I know it can. I've done it. The desire to flinch from things you don't want to think about - to derail discussions or to &quot;helpfully&quot; dig up ways to insert yourself into them as the hero or the victim or the protagonist - is something I grappled with a lot myself. You need to recognize that reaction within yourself and learn to second-guess it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, this thread is not about sexual objectification of women, it is about what I said on the topic and the first post. I treat these threads as regular conversation, topics drift, people change subjects, say things related and non related to the main topic. You know, natural flow, not some weird shit full of rules. The rules here are those of the overall forum, not what anyone wants to say they are. </div> </div> </div>You are free to discuss whatever you want. The only person, again, who has tried to silence anyone here is you. I'm glad you've changed your mind on that, but trying to project your own censorious urges on others is silly. You saw someone saying something you disliked, so you tried to think of a way to (in your own words) make them shut up; then, when people objected, you spun into a script of self-pity and blind accusations in order to try to make yourself feel better and convince yourself that you were in the right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That post was made after Isator brought Birth of the Nation as an example of abominable art that was made. It was hyperbolic and while I can't know people's minds, it seemed it was done to either invalidate my view or tag me with something very ugly. And I made this thread to respond to that. </div> </div> </div>I know. You felt personally attacked - someone disagreed with you, strongly, in a way that you didn't feel was fair. That's all right! Maybe they chose a metaphor that was a bit too harsh. But you chose to immediately leap to interpreting this as <i>censorship</i> (perhaps as a form of projection, given that your initial response to finding someone saying something you disagreed with was to try and figure out how to shut them up.) That wasn't a logically-connected response. It was an emotional response based around your defensive desire to retreat to ground that would make you the beleaguered hero or the unfairly set-upon victim.<br /> <br /> Even then, though, it was still just an attack on your arguments, not on you as a person. It might have been rude, or hyperbolic, maybe, but that's not censorship. &quot;I think what you're saying is wrong&quot; isn't censorship. &quot;I think your motivations are suspect&quot; isn't censorship. &quot;You need to stop and think about why you're saying these things, since you're not making any sense in context&quot; isn't censorship. &quot;Your opinions are bad and you should feel bad&quot; isn't censorship. And I'd go so far as to say that your abject, open desperation to define all these things as censorship - to frantically pick through the ways people have disagreed with you for bits that you can use to fall to the ground and cry &quot;HELP, HELP, I'M BEING OPPRESSED&quot; - reveals an underlying cognitive dissonance between your initial SHUT UP reaction and your honest belief that people should be able to speak.<br /> <br /> You want people saying things like Cheshire or Isator Levi did to shut up (since what they're saying is basically just &quot;I don't like this&quot;, which is an expression of their personal opinion and not something you can answer); so you <i>need</i> what they're saying to be more nefarious, more dangerous, something that can justify your gut reaction of distaste. Hence, you frantically try to interpret these things as censorship.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, unless your thoughts are completely original, or you're extremely insulated, you were probably convinced of something by someone. So arguing as if this has any kind of absolute value as to whether a point of view is valid or not is not very effective. </div> </div> </div>Arguing whether or not a point of view is valid is <i>central</i> to rational debate. Not all points of view are equally valid. Sometimes you're not seeing things clearly, either because you don't know enough or because you desperately want them to be different. When you present your point of view, it's fair to expect people to challenge it and to have to defend it. If you want to insist that your point of view is relevant and worth considering, that's something you're going to have to defend and sometimes deal with people disagreeing over.<br /> <br /> If you don't feel this way, that might explain why you feel you're constantly being censored? That is - do you actually believe it's censorship for someone to deny, dispute, or disregard your point of view? Because that's silly. Not all points of view are equal. Some are valuable; some are complicated and need a lot of thought to get the full value out of them; and some are completely worthless or pure distractions. Parsing out which ones are which is central answering hard questions.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, though, people aren't usually convinced to change their core values. Arguments get people's backs up and push them to harden their beliefs. Although I <i>hope</i> some part of this will one day get through to you, the real reason I'm doing it is not to convince you but to outline what I feel is a useful way of thinking about the problem for people who are more receptive to what I'm saying. We don't generally get our views from rational debates; after all, our reasoning is always motivated, at the end of the day, by our passions. We absorb our views, unconsciously, from our social networks - from people we respect or view as friends or are willing to listen to.<br /> <br /> I wasn't convinced to change my views. I changed because I stopped and looked back at the arguments I'd made and the positions I'd taken and asked myself <i>why</i>, and realized the reasons weren't defensible, or that they were crude emotional crutches I'd pulled together to cast myself as the hero. One day you'll either do that or you won't, and there's not much anyone else can do or say to influence that beyond hoping that you have the right sorts of people close to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are free to disagree with that, and try to convince me otherwise, or not. I hope you don't think I'm bad because of that, but you're also free to do that too. </div> </div> </div>I am, in fact, trying to address what I think is the heart of the problem here is. My basic point is that the structure of what you've said so far <i>does not make sense</i> as anything but an effort to cast yourself as the beleaguered hero the way I outlined above. Your responses so far have boiled down to various ways of saying:<br /> <br /> 1. &quot;SHUT UP. Stop talking about this here.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2. &quot;Stop trying to censor me! FREEEDOOOM!&quot;<br /> <br /> 3. &quot;Men have problems too!&quot;<br /> <br /> 4. &quot;STOP TRYING TO CENSOR ME!&quot;<br /> <br /> Aside from the initial &quot;SHUT UP&quot;, none of these have been meaningfully connected to what you were replying to. Nobody is disagreeing with your <i>right</i> to convince yourself you're the set-upon victim of this conversation, or to spin whatever disconnected fantasies you please about defending your FREEDOM from imaginary monsters who are trying to take it away from you, but as it stands those are not a coherent or meaningful argument in the context of this conversation. Given that everyone you're arguing with has tried to present their position, and that you have repeatedly attempted to parse their disagreement or criticism as censorship, I think it's easy to see why so many people feel you're being disingenuous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 06-12-2018, 05:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T07:50:53-07:00","id":1226784,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar517_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"517\" data-vbnamecard=\"517\">Aquillion</a><br /> <br /> That first quote you referenced was in this thread, which I made to elaborate more on how I feel about the things described on the topic and first post. I said nothing of the sort on the Inspirational Art Thread. So, no I didn't try to silence them where they were speaking, I made a general statement, that is all. I was talking in a whole other place about my views on it. Not badgering them, not forcing nothing down anyone's throat, not protesting, nothing of the sort. I created a place to speak my mind, as is the polite thing to do.<br /> <br /> Now if you want to follow me here and take umbrage when I express myself, and try to silence me or claim control of what I can and cannot say, outside of the terms delineated on the forum rules? What can I tell you? You don't need my permission to not speak to me or leave? Go and make yourself a thread about it? That is part of the essence of the matter anyways, maybe thats why we have a core misunderstanding about what is happening.<br /> <br /> People tried to say I can't talk about mens' issues when talking about women's issues when having a free form conversation, that is the attempt at censorship I am talking about and it happened before any talk about cleaving to this thread's topic by me.<br /> <br /> Somehow you can break the rules of the place when you feel it is appropriate, but I can't break the your rules (not the place's rules) when I feel it is appropriate.<br /> <br /> And please don't bring any real exceptional and rule breaking people into this conversation. It only makes you look like a clueless entitled and priviliged brat, belittling the existential struggle and circumstances these people suffered through, which I'm sure you loathe.<br /> <br /> I don't consider myself any sort of hero, sorry, I am very aware of the general insignificance of myself and of this conversation. Not fighting for civil rights here! Ok? This is not an existential threat to humankind, or any other lifekind of the world so... No heroes here folks! Move along.<br /> <br /> So you seem not to be reading all the posts and maintaining their content and chronology in order to respond about who said what first. I don't blame you, it is a long convuluted thread.<br /> <br /> Thank you for sharing some of your personal experience and expressing hope that I may one day make what you believe are positive changes to myself. That is a very decent and human thing to feel and say. Thank you for showing some empathy and understanding, even though I disagree with where it comes from, I do truly appreciate it.<br /> <br /> I'll add that I'm tired of the same song and the same dance, only with different partners. So if you don't have something truly new to say, and you want to talk specifically with about it, please do not make the same mistake as me and invest too much time, thought and energy on it, because it will probably not be given the same thought, time and energy in exchange, which is a pity and very wasteful for all involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 06-12-2018, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T08:33:24-07:00","id":1226798,"title":"","content":"DISCLAIMER:<br /> <br /> This is NOT the &quot;Female Sexual Objectification in Fantasy Art Discussion&quot; thread.<br /> <br /> Talking about this in a thread about freedom to produce and consume art, and the proper time and place to criticize such art, is just screaming &quot;THINK OF THE CHILDREN!&quot;. It is not central to the topic at hand, and is thread drift.<br /> <br /> This discussion is intended to be philosophical (drivel?) about freedom to produce and consume art, when and where to criticize it. If you want to argue that it is always right to criticize &quot;harmful art&quot;, that is a fair point, and we can dive into what makes art harmful, who decides said art is harmful etc...<br /> <br /> DO NOT BRING ANYONES SPECIFIC ISSUES INTO IT. They will be considered thread drift and treated as such.<br /> <br /> Please read the topic and first post to confirm what THIS thread is about.<br /> <br /> Please understand that discussion of any other matters is shifting the topic. Which I am very nonchalant about and will engage however I understand is appropriate.<br /> <br /> DO NOTE that I will not bring my issues into a platform you create to discuss your issues, as I do realize that is impolite and against the forum rules.<br /> <br /> I DO NOT CARE about your rules about why you are free to shift topics but I am not. Unless you are an elightened debater armed with objective truth, THIS WILL NOT CHANGE.<br /> <br /> If you need to label me anything you want and feel a need to tell me about it, I simply request you respect the rules and do not insult me while you're at it. I would also appreciate if you re examine these specific needs of yours, and check if anyone else already expressed similar things, before you post. If you decide not to post, that will be good, as you won't waste your time posting, and I won't waste my time refuting what you said.<br /> <br /> If you feel anything I said is against the forum rules, please invite a moderator to the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 06-12-2018, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T10:08:15-07:00","id":1226824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1226798#post1226798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DISCLAIMER:<br /> <br /> This is NOT the &quot;Female Sexual Objectification in Fantasy Art Discussion&quot; thread.<br /> <br /> Talking about this in a thread about freedom to produce and consume art, and the proper time and place to criticize such art, is just screaming &quot;THINK OF THE CHILDREN!&quot;. It is not central to the topic at hand, and is thread drift.<br /> <br /> This discussion is intended to be philosophical (drivel?) about freedom to produce and consume art, when and where to criticize it. If you want to argue that it is always right to criticize &quot;harmful art&quot;, that is a fair point, and we can dive into what makes art harmful, who decides said art is harmful etc...</div> </div> </div> </div>But the discussion that you claim to have started this thread in order to avoid derailing the other thread with <i>was</i> about sexual objectification in fantasy art. So you have now started a new thread to divert discussion of sexual objectification in fantasy art away from the inspirational art thread, and framed the thread you diverted it to in such a way that does not allow for discussion of sexual objectification in fantasy art. Do you not see the irony of complaining about people using complex rules to censor others\u2019 talking points?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-12-2018, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T10:41:37-07:00","id":1226838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1226824#post1226824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the discussion that you claim to have started this thread in order to avoid derailing the other thread about was about sexual objectification in fantasy art. So you have now started a new thread to divert discussion of sexual objectification in fantasy art away from the inspirational art thread, and framed the thread you diverted it to in such a way that does not allow for discussion of sexual objectification in fantasy art. Do you not see the irony of complaining about people using complex rules to censor others\u2019 talking points?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really Charlaquin, I started the thread to talk about Birth of the Nation, and peoples right to produce and consume things of that nature, and stuff like that, like I said on the first post...<br /> <br /> I even talked about gore and shock films and things of that nature... I wanted to discuss speech rights in regards to offensive, harmful and shocking content. It was not my intention to discuss bikini chain mail. That was a sidetrack brought on to the thread by another poster, to which I basically said;<br /> <br /> &quot;Don't forget to bring a towel...&quot; and proceeded to be Towlied.<br /> <br /> Now the argument since the beginning has been certain people can sidetrack certain subjects whenever and wherever they feel appropriate, but I can't, because reasons. To which I now say;<br /> <br /> Please read the disclaimer.<br /> <br /> People repeatedly try to force their narrative on me, I am only pointing to facts. Please see the first post. Please, What I wanted to discuss here is all spelled out there... If you want discuss other things on this thread, thats great! I'm not stickler for this, but if you wanna get into rules and regulations and stuff, I can play the game too, you know?<br /> <br /> Please stop acting like you (not only, or specifically, you, Charlaquin) know what I wanted to discuss, or why I created this thread. Besides the obvious places to figure that out that I already repeatedly pointed out (topic and first post). I have exaustively explained this since fairly early in the thread.<br /> <br /> Please stop implying that I maliciously distract from the real issue, when I left the place where the discussion was going on, and created a place to discuss what I am interested in talking about.<br /> <br /> This thread was hijacked since the first page. That doesn't mean it is about what the hijackers want it to be about.<br /> <br /> Why is it hard to understand this? Even after I repeatedly explained it?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T12:59:07-07:00","id":1226898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1226784#post1226784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That first quote you referenced was in this thread, which I made to elaborate more on how I feel about the things described on the topic and first post. I said nothing of the sort on the Inspirational Art Thread. So, no I didn't try to silence them where they were speaking, I made a general statement, that is all. I was talking in a whole other place about my views on it. Not badgering them, not forcing nothing down anyone's throat, not protesting, nothing of the sort. I created a place to speak my mind, as is the polite thing to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a quote of you summarizing what you were saying in that thread. <i>You</i> thought you were trying to get people to shut up. That was your intent. As I said, my reading is that that's been the intent behind pretty much everything you've said in this thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now if you want to follow me here and take umbrage when I express myself, and try to silence me or claim control of what I can and cannot say, outside of the terms delineated on the forum rules? </div> </div> </div>...I am having increasing trouble accepting that you are arguing in good faith at this point, since I've pointed out repeatedly that no one, at any point in this conversation, has tried to silence you. People have <i>disagreed</i> with you, and have doubted your sincerity due to the context, but that's them being free to say what they want, not them censoring you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People tried to say I can't talk about mens' issues when talking about women's issues when having a free form conversation, that is the attempt at censorship I am talking about and it happened before any talk about cleaving to this thread's topic by me. </div> </div> </div>People said that they <i>doubted your sincerity</i> because of the context in which you brought it up. That's fair for them to do. Your post leading into your discussion of men's issues ends with &quot;How tiring would it be if everytime we see a drawing of an Adonis, Hercules or Apollo, some complained like that? How relevant the complaint would be?&quot;, which, by my reading, is you saying &quot;haha, wouldn't it be absurd if people did that?&quot; In other words, it's reasonable to read that and conclude that don't actually care very much about those depictions outside of using that line of argument as a cudgel against anyone who wants to discuss the bikini-witch thing.<br /> <br /> People analyzing your argument that way in its context and coming to the conclusion that you're not arguing in good faith is not trying to silence you, that's arguing with you. Again, you seem to believe that simply disputing your viewpoint or questioning your sincerity is censoring you.<br /> <br /> It is weird. You began this conversation with, as you admitted, the overt intent of getting people you disagreed with to shut up by invoking the rules of the other thread. Then, when they refused to do so, you started saying &quot;FREEDOOOOOM&quot; and insisting that the fact that they kept criticizing stuff you liked or disagreeing with your opinions was a violation of your rights; and you tried to argue that people should stop because it would be &quot;tiring&quot; if people did the same thing with men. When people answered those arguments, you treated it as more censorship.<br /> <br /> Basically, the chain of arguments you've made and positions you've taken doesn't reflect anything that anyone else has said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I even talked about gore and shock films and things of that nature... I wanted to discuss speech rights in regards to offensive, harmful and shocking content. It was not my intention to discuss bikini chain mail. </div> </div> </div>Come on, man.<br /> <br /> By starting this thread you were trying to imply that the people you were arguing with in the first one were responding to in the other one (especially Isator Levi, who you called out by name, but also, implicitly, anyone who says they feel bikini-witch art is sometimes gratuitous) was pushing for censorship and opposed FREEEEEDOM\u2122. That was a groundless argument that had no relation to what anyone else was saying, and people responded appropriately.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll add that I'm tired of the same song and the same dance, only with different partners. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps this is the problem. It feels as if this discussion is mostly you shadow-boxing the imaginary version of your opponents that you've built out of the worst things people have been said to you in previous arguments. No one but you has brought up censorship, or tried to silence people, or tried to take away your FREEEEEDOM\u2122, yet you continuously circle back around to it. <i>Why</i> hold on to that? &quot;No, we're not trying to censor you; everyone here likes freedom just as much as you&quot; should be something that makes you happy, not something you bullheadedly ignore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 06-12-2018, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T13:09:54-07:00","id":1226902,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar517_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"517\" data-vbnamecard=\"517\">Aquillion</a><br /> <br /> Yeah, ok Aquillion, thank you for being so knowledgeable about me and telling me what I'm actually thinking or thought.<br /> <br /> Here I was thinking I was an expert on myself, but lo and behold, you show up and dazzle me, showing me insights about myself I never imagined!<br /> <br /> AMAZING!<br /> <br /> PS: All the rest is just repeat though, I'm sad, for your and my wasted time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2746,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","user":"TGUEIROS","date":". 06-12-2018, 04:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T15:01:35-07:00","id":1226948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1226902#post1226902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here I was thinking I was an expert on myself\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Even experts can be shown things about their field they weren't aware of, that they never would have discovered on their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-12T17:13:14-07:00","id":1226977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1225302-art-criticism-and-freedom-contains-disturbing-topics-please-be-aware?p=1226948#post1226948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even experts can be shown things about their field they weren't aware of, that they never would have discovered on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow! What a clean and truthful counterpoint!<br /> <br /> You are very right, that was a shallow argument to make. I got carried away in trying to be funny and ended up weakening my stance. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Thanks!<br /> <br /> /hattip<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T14:11:36-07:00","id":1227518,"title":"","content":"Anyway, so interesting thing recently: I was acquainted with the trailer for the upcoming new Devil May Cry game, in which the new supporting character of Nico was introduced. She's apparently a gunsmith and engineer.<br /> <br /> \u200bShe's kind of absurdly sexualised, with skimpy clothing, lots of tattoos, and a moment in the trailer in which she catches a cigarette in her mouth, in slow motion, while driving a van that is tumbling over.<br /> <br /> \u200bI considered it a bit, and found that I'm sort of... okay with that? It's not really out of place in the overall over-the-top absurdity of the game series. That's not saying that there's an equivalence between her and some of the male characters, just that when all is said and done there is <i>some</i> place for priorities like that, and I feel as though something with the tone of that series might be it.<br /> <br /> \u200bMind, my perspective might be influenced a bit by my having looked around other parts of the Internet reacting to the character, and seeing some of the bro types and Gamergaters who <i>hate</i> her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T03:22:27-07:00","id":1227615,"title":"","content":"Had to look her up. Anyway, wouldn't call her <i>absurdly</i> sexualized. <br /> <br /> Sure, she is thin, white and half-naked, but she has tattoos and glasses. Oh, and from what I could see from the trailer a personality. So, eh, while there's definitely room for improvement, like wearing actual pants or something, could be a lot worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-15T07:44:28-07:00","id":1227654,"title":"","content":"At some point she demands payment for her services/product, which means that she's expressing a power over Nero, and those bro types hate it when women dare to exercise any sort of power (in this case, having something the male character wants). Obviously she should just offer things up freely and submit herself as a servant to Nero/the (presumably male) player, because that's the only role those kinds of players believe women should occupy.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I say &quot;presumably male&quot; not because I think that gamers are presumably going to be male (I don't respect anybody who tries to defend their entitled, sexist beliefs with &quot;But only <i>males</i> play video games!&quot;) but as part of the strawman that I created to represent people bitching about her.<br /> <br /> It's totally possible that somebody might find her grating. I'm not sure how I feel about her accent, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":1923,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","user":"BigDamnHero","date":". 06-15-2018, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}